{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions","id":317776,"title":"Not So Frequently Asked Questions!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-20T16:50:12-08:00","id":317776,"title":"Not So Frequently Asked Questions!","content":"Okay, so Ghouls are counted as having a Blood Potency of 0. I am curious, does this allow them to &quot;feed&quot; on animals as a source of Vitae?<br /> <br /> Also, Nossie deformities, for those of us going at it old school. Do they only manifest when the Lonely Curse sets in, i.e. when the Haunt reaches Humanity 6? Or are they present from embrace, just without the mechanical effects until they degenerate accordingly?<br /> <br /> When a Kindred riding the wave bites a grappled opponent, can they opt not to take the automatic blood point since they are more in control of the Frenzy?<br /> <br /> I'll probably have more to add to this thread over time, but these will do for now. Thanks in advance, developers!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1353-riche","name":"RichE","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T17:09:52-08:00","id":317808,"title":"","content":"1) Ghouls cannot feed, they require kindred to provide Vitae for them.<br /> <br /> 2) Reasonably speaking yes, as the penalties thematically arise from the deformity. I would, however, give them a light version of it even at high humanity and never allow them to take the higher version of Striking Looks.<br /> <br /> 3) A vampire riding the wave is still barely in control, they can provide direction but that level of restraint shouldn't be possible in frenzy.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T17:18:11-08:00","id":317810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=317808#post317808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Reasonably speaking yes, as the penalties thematically arise from the deformity. I would, however, give them a light version of it even at high humanity and never allow them to take the higher version of Striking Looks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? Striking Looks isn't about having an attractive appearance, it's about having one you can leverage socially.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;These are merely stones...&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/276-merkonan","name":"Merkonan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar276_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T17:35:15-08:00","id":317815,"title":"","content":"Hrmmm, fair enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T02:16:29-08:00","id":318103,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but in PenDragon's defense it used to be just being pretty, that will go against the concept of the deformed Nosferatu (wich is only a posibility among many).<br /> <br /> The new Striking Looks can be a perfect fit for a deformed Nosferatu though, as you can just asociate it to the Intimidate Skill for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T05:31:30-08:00","id":318175,"title":"","content":"I'm waiting for David and/or Rose to give their two cents. Mostly because I don't want this to devolve into a thread of &quot;Pretty Nossies are doing it wrung!&quot;, for whatever reason. ;p","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1353-riche","name":"RichE","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T07:20:50-08:00","id":318228,"title":"","content":"I think a way it could work for nosferatu is that they always have their deformity, albeit maybe less pronounced but until they reach 6 in humanity, people don't hold it against them. If you think about it, the mechanical result can make people seem rather shallow. If you met someone whose eyes weren't level, you wouldn't necessarily treat him any worse for it, but if that person was a nosferatu with lowered humanity, it would look wrong on more than a physical level, perhaps because you're then aware in some way that you're looking at a manifestation of the Beast and not one of the sexy ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T08:17:25-08:00","id":318264,"title":"","content":"Hey, Pretty Nossies have <i>history</i>.<br /> <br /> The Galloi say hi (I might have to update the Galloi to GMC. They're pretty great.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T08:40:57-08:00","id":318275,"title":"","content":"Personally, I would say if you want to go the &quot;all nos are deformed&quot; route, I would say more power to you, but that the mechanical effect of the clan bane is caused by something other than physical appearance. They may be disfigured and terrifying from the moment of embrace, but that alone doesn't cause them to count their Humanity lower for the sake of interactions with mortals. It may or may not add other penalties and bonuses to certain rolls, Nos clanbook style, at ST discretion, but that's purely the result of their physical appearance. When their humanity drops and their bane kicks in, that's something beyond just their looks; something altogether more supernatural, that causes them to make mortals uncomfortable in a way their deformities alone never could. Almost like they can't fully control their predatory aura and they're always giving off a low-level sign that &quot;I'm not human and you should fear me&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T08:43:20-08:00","id":318279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=318264#post318264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, Pretty Nossies have <i>history</i>.<br /> <br /> The Galloi say hi (I might have to update the Galloi to GMC. They're pretty great.)</div> </div> </div> </div>One of my favorite characters I've played, and still like to dust off from time to time is a Galloi. I made her for a LARP originally, and it actually helped me come to terms with my own gender identity in many ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T15:57:56-08:00","id":318547,"title":"","content":"Nosferatu with deformities only gain those deformities as the curse sets in. It can be a dramatic moment after a breaking point, as the vampire's face twists into a horror mask or his skin splits like rotten fruit.<br /> <br /> I'm cool with Nosferatu having GMC-era Striking Looks. There are probably some Nosferatu concepts where it's a bad idea, but that's the kind of thing you settle on a character-by-character basis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T17:33:12-08:00","id":318577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=318547#post318547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nosferatu with deformities only gain those deformities as the curse sets in. It can be a dramatic moment after a breaking point, as the vampire's face twists into a horror mask or his skin splits like rotten fruit.<br /> <br /> I'm cool with Nosferatu having GMC-era Striking Looks. There are probably some Nosferatu concepts where it's a bad idea, but that's the kind of thing you settle on a character-by-character basis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nosferatu were literally the main reason I changed Striking Looks, so it isn't explicitly &quot;pretty&quot; now. And I think a Merit called &quot;Striking Looks&quot; should fit someone with a Discipline called &quot;Nightmare&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T17:57:56-08:00","id":318589,"title":"","content":"A what a good change it is!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T00:58:43-08:00","id":318788,"title":"","content":"Also, here's a suggestion: Want a deformed nosferatu? One who looks like a monster from the get go? The weakness seems too weak? Slap a Persistent Condition on him. That way, he get's penalties and reactions appropriate to his looks, while also rewarding the player with Beats for choosing (or getting ) such a nosferatu.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T06:49:45-08:00","id":319852,"title":"","content":"I thank both David and Rose for the answers on the Nossie stuff. Guessing the questions on Ghouls munching on animals and the Riding the Wave thing were answered well enough by PenDragon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1353-riche","name":"RichE","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T09:01:05-08:00","id":319930,"title":"","content":"To drift away from the Pretty Nossies question and back to the primary purpose of the thread...<br /> <br /> What's the purpose of the Masquerade/Requiem? I'm genuinely looking at them and wondering how they fit into the design space; what parts of theme and setting they best fit. My natural interpretation is that it's meant to emphasize that a vampire can never truly have peace between their humanity and their beast; that to feed the other, they must take on a role that's truly separate from who they feel they are.<br /> <br /> Is that the only interpretation, though? Is there something I'm missing? How can they be emphasized?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T09:26:20-08:00","id":319939,"title":"","content":"Are you referring to Mask and Dirge?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T09:58:35-08:00","id":320002,"title":"","content":"Right. Those things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T10:56:53-08:00","id":320039,"title":"","content":"Mask is a role you perform in the world. It's not necessarily entirely fake, but it's the medium through which you turn being dead into some kind of a life.<br /> <br /> Dirge is who you are when no one's watching, or when you don't care who's watching. It's not necessarily entirely secret, but it's what happens when your real self bubbles to the surface. It's the life you lead inside your head.<br /> <br /> Depending on what Mask and Dirge you pick, you'll highlight different themes of the game. However, they generally represent the vampire's need to perform an identity for the world around her, while not neglecting the Requiem that comes naturally to her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T14:13:20-08:00","id":320185,"title":"","content":"The way I often explain it is that your Mask is how you want people to see you, and your Dirge is how you see yourself. Its an oversimplification, but I find it helps newer players wrap their heads around the concept. On a deeper level, it's about the double-life vampires have to live. For obvious reasons, they can't reveal their true thoughts or feelings in the company of mortals, and even within vampire society, they have a lot of social pressure to not come across as a complete monster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T02:28:05-08:00","id":335902,"title":"","content":"Okay, so in the event Diablerie becomes a thing in our Baltimore game, I am curious, can any of the Covenant specific disciplines, or the Mysteries of the OD be gained through that means? With Cruac and Theban it's probably a no brainer given they are described as Disciplines in their fluff, but for the Mysteries, it's a bit different, and the only thing they have in common is how they scale and points costs. This may be one to be added to the FAQ, if answered, as it seems like an important enough question for chronicles where diablerists abound.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1353-riche","name":"RichE","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T02:47:37-08:00","id":335906,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't allow any of those to be gained trough Diablerie. Why, you ask? Both Mysteries and Blood Sorcery are not &quot;natural&quot; powers of vampires, they are things that were learned and practice to be able to be used, they don't come as easy as the 10 Disciplines. Also, if Diablerizing a Crone, Sanctified or Dragon was the only thing preventing you from getting their Covenant secrets... that would make for a very boring scenario.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T09:53:57-08:00","id":336125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichE</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions#post317776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so Ghouls are counted as having a Blood Potency of 0. I am curious, does this allow them to &quot;feed&quot; on animals as a source of Vitae?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ghouls are not vampires, they are humans with access to a handful of vampire abilities, mostly disciplines and near immortality. So they do not automatically convert blood into vitae upon drinking it. It comes from feeding on vampires directly.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 12-10-2014, 12:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T11:17:01-08:00","id":336171,"title":"","content":"I was just thinking about the Blood-Cleansing Ritual, and I began to wonder something. And victims of a Blood-Bond capable of being aware of what's happening to them? And, more importantly, can they WANT to be free from it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T17:19:28-08:00","id":336493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=335906#post335906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, if Diablerizing a Crone, Sanctified or Dragon was the only thing preventing you from getting their Covenant secrets... that would make for a very boring scenario.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd respond to the point about these not being &quot;natural&quot; powers of the Vampire by noting that Diablerie also lets you gain a skill, which means that you could devour someone's soul and suddenly know how to fix a Volkswagen, but that's not as important a point to address as this one; Rule of Fun is danged important, after all.<br /> <br /> I sort of agree with you in that simply going around diablerizing vampires for power is a dull way to get access to that power, but I think there's right ways for it to be done and, moreover, all the more intriguing consequences for it. After all, the Ordo Dracul seeks to evolve a vampire, and what might consuming what is essentially a self-altering curse do to someone? Devouring the soul of one of the Sanctified means you just swallowed a literal servant of God, and the Old Testament God at that. That's going to have interesting consequences, ranging from God smiting your city with a plague (is it purely mundane, and thus reduces feeding opportunities, or does the vengeful wrath of the Divine lay the city low too?) to angels of wrath showing up to wreck your biz. The Crone, meanwhile, is a predatory force of nature; I imagine she'd probably respect someone who devoured her children as much as anything. Respect them so much, in fact, that she might wish to bless them more and more until they beg her to stop.<br /> <br /> In other words, I think there's plenty of fun to be had. It's just the kind of fun that has consequences. Naturally, the consequences don't have to be entirely destructive, though; a player character who survives to come out the other side may be much stronger for it. It's just gonna make their unlife <i>really</i> interesting for a while, and explain why the hell no-one else ever does this.<br /> <br /> You could also include it requiring you to learn a special technique, if you wanted, and allow them to only learn further dots via Diablerie.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=336171#post336171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was just thinking about the Blood-Cleansing Ritual, and I began to wonder something. And victims of a Blood-Bond capable of being aware of what's happening to them? And, more importantly, can they WANT to be free from it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Are victims capable of knowing what's happening to them? Absolutely. Can they want to be free from it? Most certainly. However, I'd compare it to, say, someone having a powerfully addictive drug slipped into their morning coffee. Are they innately aware of what's happening? No. Can they want to break the addiction once it's formed? Certainly. Will they want to? Maybe. Maybe not.<br /> <br /> It all comes down to circumstance and the individual involved. The Blood Bond is all-consuming obsession but it's not <i>love</i>. That much is patently clear. You can want something so badly that you hate it; you can crave something while knowing it's awful for you; you can desperately want to be free of something that you desire without restraint.<br /> <br /> For some ghouls, the Blood Bond is something they never understand. All they know is that their regnant is the most amazing thing they've ever encountered; meeting them was pivotal. There's time before they met their regnant and there's now.<br /> <br /> For one of the Kindred, however, who is likely well aware of what the Bond is, it's a hateful thing. Icky sticky obsession with someone, a fearfulness of losing them, and the full awareness that they're <i>making</i> you feel this way? Not fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2855,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","user":"Axelgear","date":".  Adding another reply 12-10-2014, 08:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T19:54:20-08:00","id":336627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=335906#post335906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't allow any of those to be gained trough Diablerie. Why, you ask? Both Mysteries and Blood Sorcery are not &quot;natural&quot; powers of vampires, they are things that were learned and practice to be able to be used, they don't come as easy as the 10 Disciplines. Also, if Diablerizing a Crone, Sanctified or Dragon was the only thing preventing you from getting their Covenant secrets... that would make for a very boring scenario.</div> </div> </div> </div>An interesting answer with a viewpoint that mirrors my own. The main reason I ask is because the book seems to give no indication one way or the other. And while some of the questions I ask might seem a bit more common sense (read:ghouls eating animals), others aren't so clear cut due to a less detailed writing when it comes to those things.<br /> <br /> With that in mind, while I do respect the opinion of other players who would disallow such things in their own chronicles, I am waiting to hear the official word from Dave and/or Rose, as I notice they tend to differ on what they do or don't intend with the rules, and I am interested in hearing what they say on the matter before I consider anything &quot;canon&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1353-riche","name":"RichE","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T22:48:52-08:00","id":336786,"title":"","content":"Unique bloodline disciplines can no longer be learned through diablerie so I think Coils which are never actually indicated to be disciplines would fall into the same category. They also are more of a change in the vampire rather than a learned ability. I wouldn't allow blood sorcery disciplines to be learned by anyone that isn't a member of the respective covenant or has the discipline already because you have to be in the covenant to learn rituals. What good is a discipline that you can't use? I think you are better off taking the skill option. If you allow improvised rituals then it is worth considering. It might have been left ambiguous for that reason. The Coils never being referenced as disciplines speaks for itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T17:21:38-08:00","id":337572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=336786#post336786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unique bloodline disciplines can no longer be learned through diablerie...</div> </div> </div> </div>No longer? I wasn't aware bloodline disciplines could be learned outside of that bloodline (barring taught ghouls or niche bloodlines).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1230-thenagain","name":"thenagain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T17:51:31-08:00","id":337593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenagain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=337572#post337572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No longer? I wasn't aware bloodline disciplines could be learned outside of that bloodline (barring taught ghouls or niche bloodlines).</div> </div> </div> </div>In VtR, If you didn't belong to a specific bloodline and you diablerized a bloodline member with the signature unique discipline, if you weren't already in another bloodline and were a clan candidate to join it, you could potentially get avused into that bloodline and learn the bloodline unique discipline via diablerie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","name":"Audrey St. John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T03:03:10-08:00","id":337905,"title":"","content":"I wasn't aware of that. Is it in the Bloodlines the Chosen apendix? I remeber it having alternative ways of being inducted into a Bloodline, but I didn't remeber that one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T09:18:07-08:00","id":338098,"title":"","content":"The VtR book specifically mentions diablerie as a method of joining a bloodline and that if you are a bloodline member then you could also obtain the bloodline discipline via diablerie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","name":"Audrey St. John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T06:46:29-08:00","id":338998,"title":"","content":"And I shall continue to needle the developers for answers! I mainly am curious because I feel allowing such somewhat dilutes the interesting roleplay that comes from playing a member of the OD. I mean, I was keeping myself fairly reserved when it comes to my reasoning, and not going into too much detail, but the thing with the OD is they're about the student mentor relationship, and until told otherwise, I shall believe that is the case in 2nd Edition. If Vamps are allowed to just go about sucking coils out of each other, than what's the point in even trying for that student mentor relationship when folks can just diablerize and get that stuff lickety split, you know?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1353-riche","name":"RichE","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T06:54:53-08:00","id":338999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichE</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=338998#post338998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I shall continue to needle the developers for answers! I mainly am curious because I feel allowing such somewhat dilutes the interesting roleplay that comes from playing a member of the OD. I mean, I was keeping myself fairly reserved when it comes to my reasoning, and not going into too much detail, but the thing with the OD is they're about the student mentor relationship, and until told otherwise, I shall believe that is the case in 2nd Edition. If Vamps are allowed to just go about sucking coils out of each other, than what's the point in even trying for that student mentor relationship when folks can just diablerize and get that stuff lickety split, you know?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there's the fact that the penalties for Diablerie <i>really suck</i>, but I understand where you're coming from. Still, it seems silly that you could theoretically steal a Skill dot from your target through Diablerie, even if that skill is, say, Academics or Science but <i>not </i>steal Blood Sorcery or Scales.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T12:53:49-08:00","id":341080,"title":"","content":"So, I can't seem to find the new Vampire: the Requiem book (Blood and Smoke/Second Edition) isn't available on drivethrurpg. I bought the PDF a bit ago and was looking to get the book as a Christmas present for a friend. Is it available elsewhere, or a planned re-release of it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T13:35:33-08:00","id":342182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=341080#post341080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I can't seem to find the new Vampire: the Requiem book (Blood and Smoke/Second Edition) isn't available on drivethrurpg. I bought the PDF a bit ago and was looking to get the book as a Christmas present for a friend. Is it available elsewhere, or a planned re-release of it?</div> </div> </div> </div>We took it down temporarily while we proof the new PoD. It should be back up soon; we ended up a bit delayed because there was a problem with the first proof.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T13:37:07-08:00","id":342185,"title":"","content":"Here's what I said via PM on the diablerie topic:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Powers that are based on knowledge and experience can be gained via diablerie. That covers Cruac and Theban Sorcery. I'd usually say it <i>doesn't</i> include the Coils of the Dragon, because they involve things like experimenting on yourself in addition to learning. But if a character achieved their rank in a Coil primarily by meditation, it might transfer via diablerie. Oaths and Law can't be transferred via diablerie, because they require things outside the character (like agreement to an oath to a specific person) in order to work. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T14:36:37-08:00","id":342290,"title":"","content":"In my games i would rule out also Cruac and Theban Sorcery because i would say they require not only knowledge and experience, but also a personal spiritual belief component (that varies fro kindred to kindred), that you can't obtain through diablerie. If it is just a matter of knowing the ritual and enacting it to have it take effect, why would you need a certain degree of mastery to cast high level rituals or a minimum/maximum score of humanity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2213,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2213-tittopaolo210","user":"TittoPaolo210","date":". 12-16-2014, 05:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2213-tittopaolo210","name":"TittoPaolo210","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T16:12:27-08:00","id":342378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TittoPaolo210</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=342290#post342290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my games i would rule out also Cruac and Theban Sorcery because i would say they require not only knowledge and experience, but also a personal spiritual belief component (that varies fro kindred to kindred), that you can't obtain through diablerie. If it is just a matter of knowing the ritual and enacting it to have it take effect, why would you need a certain degree of mastery to cast high level rituals or a minimum/maximum score of humanity?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Because the knowledge of said rituals caps your humanity, and because for the ritual to work you need humanity of at least X, respectively <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And the degree of mastery, is the same as for other things... you know the actions for dominate, look someone in the eye and command... that doesn't mean that you can repeat it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T17:22:44-08:00","id":342404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=342378#post342378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Because the knowledge of said rituals caps your humanity, and because for the ritual to work you need humanity of at least X, respectively <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And the degree of mastery, is the same as for other things... you know the actions for dominate, look someone in the eye and command... that doesn't mean that you can repeat it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I always imagined the humanity part of ritual disciplines represent spiritual investment in the discipline, not just numbers requirements<br /> <br /> Cruac doesn't cap your humanity just because you know a ritual (not even some truly horrible scales or diablerie, that is the ultimate wickedness, can cap your humanity, why just knowing some procedure would?), it caps your humanity because you have to get THAT close to your beast to commune with it and harvest the power of its blood. To really know the ritual, just learning the procedure isn't enough, you have to craft that close connection for yourself, and it's a thing diablerie can't steal.<br /> <br /> Theban Sorcery requires you to have a minimum humanity because it works with your rational human mind, the part of you that dreams, that makes plan, that cares and, most of all, has the power to believe (whereas the beast cares only about safety and blood), the farther away you get from that enlightened state of mind the harder it is for the power of your beliefs to call that higher power that gives you miracles and that pure state of mind of true belief is also something you can't steal with diablerie.<br /> <br /> Dominate is a power ventrue develop naturally, without investment sometimes, just by the process of becoming vampires. Learning blood sorcery feels a lot more deep than that.<br /> <br /> At least, that's how i picture them, i feel that being able to get blood sorcery dots from diablerie kind of detracts from the deep spiritual themes i like to evoke with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2213,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2213-tittopaolo210","user":"TittoPaolo210","date":". 12-16-2014, 08:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2213-tittopaolo210","name":"TittoPaolo210","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T21:54:42-08:00","id":342602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=342182#post342182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We took it down temporarily while we proof the new PoD. It should be back up soon; we ended up a bit delayed because there was a problem with the first proof.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks for the response!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T05:32:13-08:00","id":342835,"title":"","content":"And why can't Diablerie get you closer to the beast and teach you to commune with the beast for Cruac? As your example shows. What Diablerie does best is connect you with your beast <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> And why can't Diablerie teach you of faith required for Theban?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T05:45:56-08:00","id":342840,"title":"","content":"Technically, it's using Theban Sorcery that requires an effort of will that channels not the Beast but the Man (if it requires true faith as well is debatable). Just learning about it has nothing to do with that. Knowledge is knowledge, and that is something you can obtain through Diablerie. Now, the Coils are more subjective, but I would rule it's perfectly possible to obtain knowledge of <i>how</i> to achieve a Coil through Diablerie, and enact the change manually, as opposed to gaining it immediately.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T07:27:10-08:00","id":342900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=336171#post336171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was just thinking about the Blood-Cleansing Ritual, and I began to wonder something. And victims of a Blood-Bond capable of being aware of what's happening to them? And, more importantly, can they WANT to be free from it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course you can be aware of it. But as the book explains it, a blood bond creates an artificial sense of true love. You may know your master is a heartless monster. You may recognize they're abusing you. But you still care for them deeply and would do anything for them, hoping in vain that you can be the one who changes them!<br /> <br /> At that point, being aware of it is probably worse than blissful ignorance!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T08:45:24-08:00","id":342965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=342835#post342835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And why can't Diablerie get you closer to the beast and teach you to commune with the beast for Cruac? As your example shows. What Diablerie does best is connect you with your beast <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> And why can't Diablerie teach you of faith required for Theban?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the ability to commune with the beast or harvest the power of the man is not simply about knowledge that you can teach or obtain through diablerie, it's about insight that you have to research yourself.<br /> <br /> Of course, this is how i rule it, not how it should be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=342840#post342840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically, it's using Theban Sorcery that requires an effort of will that channels not the Beast but the Man (if it requires true faith as well is debatable). Just learning about it has nothing to do with that. Knowledge is knowledge, and that is something you can obtain through Diablerie. Now, the Coils are more subjective, but I would rule it's perfectly possible to obtain knowledge of <i>how</i> to achieve a Coil through Diablerie, and enact the change manually, as opposed to gaining it immediately.</div> </div> </div> </div>I equated the effort of will with faith in my argument, i should have been more accurate, my bad. Of course i would rule it's possible to learn how to achieve a coil, or even learn a new ritual through diablerie. I'd say diablerie could be a step in learning a new dot in blood sorcery, but it's not enough to develop a new dot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2213-tittopaolo210","name":"TittoPaolo210","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T08:56:37-08:00","id":343005,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry but how does Insight differ from Knowledge and where is it written that Insight cannot be gained from diablerie? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> You can rule it whatever the way you want, however claiming that it's how it should be, when the rules say otherwise is not the way to go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T09:18:42-08:00","id":343025,"title":"","content":"There is kind of a difference between <i>&quot;this is subjective so I rule it this way&quot;</i> and <i>&quot;this is objective but I'd rather rule it this way because it makes more sense/has more appeal to me&quot;</i>, yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T09:39:40-08:00","id":343050,"title":"","content":"While I said &quot;knowledge and experience&quot; above, lots of other things can be transmitted by diablerie. It can change your personality in ways we don't quantify in mechanics, like leading you towards faith. You get a little bit of your victim inside you, and that can change who you are.<br /> <br /> Which isn't to say not to adjust things to your group's taste.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T10:33:36-08:00","id":343081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=343050#post343050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I said &quot;knowledge and experience&quot; above, lots of other things can be transmitted by diablerie. It can change your personality in ways we don't quantify in mechanics, like leading you towards faith. You get a little bit of your victim inside you, and that can change who you are.<br /> <br /> Which isn't to say not to adjust things to your group's taste.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I got the feeling this was intended, I was not so sure from the way things were presented. The victim's influence on you seemed to vanish after you got rid of the Tainted Condition somehow. I do rather like the interpretation with the permanent change, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T12:21:25-08:00","id":343137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=343081#post343081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I got the feeling this was intended, I was not so sure from the way things were presented. The victim's influence on you seemed to vanish after you got rid of the Tainted Condition somehow. I do rather like the interpretation with the permanent change, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>The most overt symptoms go away with the Tainted Condition, but you can end up really changed or scarred. The Storytelling system doesn't provide a lot of hooks to model personality traits at a finer-grained level than Virtue/Vice/Mask/Dirge, but the fact that your dots change reflects that you've been permanently altered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 12-17-2014, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T01:09:53-08:00","id":343728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=343005#post343005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry but how does Insight differ from Knowledge and where is it written that Insight cannot be gained from diablerie? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> You can rule it whatever the way you want, however claiming that it's how it should be, when the rules say otherwise is not the way to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the difference between an artist and an art scholar: if the scholar lacks the spark of the artist, he can study the rules and the techniques, he KNOWS them but he'll never be able to use them with INSIGHT to create new arts.<br /> <br /> Also, did i type incorrectly? i said that i like it to use them this way, not that's how the rules say it should be. Rose has been pretty clear on what the rules are and i certainly am not someone who will tell her something different xD.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=343050#post343050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I said &quot;knowledge and experience&quot; above, lots of other things can be transmitted by diablerie. It can change your personality in ways we don't quantify in mechanics, like leading you towards faith. You get a little bit of your victim inside you, and that can change who you are.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't considered this, but then, why can't you get coils the same way, since they too are a pretty relevant part of the victim?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2213,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2213-tittopaolo210","user":"TittoPaolo210","date":".  Fixed the quote 12-18-2014, 05:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2213-tittopaolo210","name":"TittoPaolo210","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T02:10:05-08:00","id":343746,"title":"","content":"Coils are a transformation. You could gain the knowledge and experience of someone that learned a Coil but that would not impart the changes that would occur when learning the Coil. You might have an argument about being able to buy the Coil without the prerequisites. Coils are too intrinsic to a particular person. It would be like gaining, and retaining, a person's memories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T02:18:28-08:00","id":343748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TittoPaolo210</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=343728#post343728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the difference between an artist and an art scholar: if the scholar lacks the spark of the artist, he can study the rules and the techniques, he KNOWS them but he'll never be able to use them with INSIGHT to create new arts.</div> </div> </div> </div>And Diablerie can perfectly transmit the Insight of this said artist to the diablerist, so he feels the art, more than he knows it. Thus increasing his Crafts dots, but in a different way, by giving him the INSIGHT you're talking about and not the KNOWLEDGE.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T02:36:07-08:00","id":343761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=343748#post343748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And Diablerie can perfectly transmit the Insight of this said artist to the diablerist, so he feels the art, more than he knows it. Thus increasing his Crafts dots, but in a different way, by giving him the INSIGHT you're talking about and not the KNOWLEDGE.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then why can't i learn coils from diablerie? If diablerie can change both the forma mentis and the physical nature of your curse, coils should be no different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2213-tittopaolo210","name":"TittoPaolo210","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T03:18:56-08:00","id":343767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TittoPaolo210</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=343761#post343761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then why can't i learn coils from diablerie? If diablerie can change both the forma mentis and the physical nature of your curse, coils should be no different.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because Dragons are special little snowflakes and the Coils of the Dragon are a sacred cow that nobody except a Dragon should be able to obtain under any circumstance and must be taught by another Dragon. The fact that learning them is cheaper to gain xp wise is proof of their specialness, not that they're actually easier for someone to learn and implement than a 'real' discipline or blood sorcery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","name":"Audrey St. John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T04:11:33-08:00","id":343778,"title":"","content":"Where did I mention that diablerie changes physical nature of your curse? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Insight ain't a physical part of the curse...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T07:38:35-08:00","id":343901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=343778#post343778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where did I mention that diablerie changes physical nature of your curse? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Insight ain't a physical part of the curse...</div> </div> </div> </div>Learning clan specific disciplines is about changing the nature of your blood to develop them, or physical skills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2213-tittopaolo210","name":"TittoPaolo210","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T12:16:53-08:00","id":344026,"title":"","content":"Are there any plans to answer questions regarding the clanbooks - the nature of Felix (other than what we know from Fall of the Camarilla), the identity of those who set the project in motion, etc.?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T12:41:37-08:00","id":344033,"title":"","content":"If you train in acrobatics then you would represent that by dots in athletics and dexterity, possibly other skills and attributes. Unless you were naturally talented to the point that the improvement was minimal, you would increase attributes to represent the effect of the training. If you stole the knowledge from someone that went through the training then you could get the skill increase, but you would not get an increase in dexterity. That is an approximation of learning a Coil.<br /> <br /> After researching, meditating, experimenting and everything else you learned part of a Coil so you get a dot. The mechanics represent the &quot;enlightenment.&quot; If you steal knowledge of it then you know how to get there, but you didn't go there yourself. Your body was not trained to behave as it should so you don't actually have the power. You only know how to get it. A player could argue they should be able to buy it at that point. That is house rule territory.<br /> <br /> Clan specific disciplines can be learned by anyone. Bloodlines not tied to the specific clan can learn them as their bloodline discipline. All it takes is the &quot;insight&quot; from the blood of someone that knows what you want to learn. Diablerie would include the blood needed to learn and the act gives you the experience so you get a dot.<br /> <br /> It costs the same experience to learn a Coil as any other discipline, but it also takes time to learn a Coil. Coils are more difficult to learn than other disciplines. Unique bloodline disciplines require joining the bloodline to learn. Coils are closer to that than any of the other disciplines.<br /> <br /> It would be like a player saying they could change into an animal after learning Protean 3 despite their character never consuming an animal before. They only did part of the required activities. There is no justification to say if you diablerized to get the Protean that you could change into the animals the one drained could change into. You could allow it to work that way, but that would simply be relaxation of rules to get a desired result. That is definitely house rule territory.<br /> <br /> You could say that you can diablerize and get a Coil dot if you practice if for a month, but that is house rule territory. A Scale is more like a traditional discipline dot. You can justify gaining that with diablerie. A blood ritual can be justified. Sorcery would be a stretch, but you wouldn't be completely out there. Getting a Coil without putting in the time to train pushes into the realm of credulity. If you can learn Coils from diablerie then you should be able to learn unique bloodline disciplines from diablerie. You should be able to get merits from diablerie - Claws of the Unholy. It gets out of hand quickly.<br /> <br /> Edit: In case it was lost. You don't need justification. It is a game. If it makes things fun then house rule away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":". 12-18-2014, 08:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T12:56:22-08:00","id":344037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TittoPaolo210</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=343728#post343728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't considered this, but then, why can't you get coils the same way, since they too are a pretty relevant part of the victim?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, to me, Coils potentially involve doing weird stuff to your body, which doesn't seem like something diablerie should transfer. A diablerizing vampire doesn't get her victim's scars (although that would potentially be cool). As I said originally, if a vampire achieved Coil dots purely through meditation or some other sort of internal change, it makes sense that they'd transfer. Probably also if they did it by changing the nature of their soul, for example with the help of a sorcerer or mage.<br /> <br /> It's not that big a deal, though. If I were running a chronicle where diablerie was less taboo than normal, and stealing covenant advantages was a key tactic in, for example, the city power struggle, then I might rule the other way. I might also do that if a player <i>really</i> wanted a dot in a Coil... I don't worry that much about covenant advantage bleedover when it's the PCs doing it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=344026#post344026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any plans to answer questions regarding the clanbooks - the nature of Felix (other than what we know from Fall of the Camarilla), the identity of those who set the project in motion, etc.?</div> </div> </div> </div>The short answer is that this depends entirely on what CCP greenlights. It's also worth mentioning that I have a contemporary story about Felix, sans Dracula, which is looking for a home.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T23:11:36-08:00","id":344426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=344037#post344037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, to me, Coils potentially involve doing weird stuff to your body, which doesn't seem like something diablerie should transfer. A diablerizing vampire doesn't get her victim's scars (although that would potentially be cool). As I said originally, if a vampire achieved Coil dots purely through meditation or some other sort of internal change, it makes sense that they'd transfer. Probably also if they did it by changing the nature of their soul, for example with the help of a sorcerer or mage.<br /> <br /> It's not that big a deal, though. If I were running a chronicle where diablerie was less taboo than normal, and stealing covenant advantages was a key tactic in, for example, the city power struggle, then I might rule the other way. I might also do that if a player <i>really</i> wanted a dot in a Coil... I don't worry that much about covenant advantage bleedover when it's the PCs doing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose the one issue here is in a setting where the means are less important than the end. Which would never be a setting I run, but those sort of settings do exist. In places where justification is irrelevant, or, say, people are just wanting to cleanse a chat's database and just have inactive PCs fall into a torpor they cannot wake from, and the remaining PCs are allowed to diablerize them, there's very litle to say just how the victim actually obtained that dot in a coil which is transferred to the diablerist. So what you get is a place where diablerie of coils could be as common as the diablerie of any other discipline,should inactive PCs become more common, and such inexplicable means to explain their absence become just as common.<br /> <br /> Though I suppose if that is the sort of story those STs wish to run, there is little which can be done about it. And I guess as with some folks have said on this topic, if people don't want it to be that way, the ST has every right to not make it as much of a free ride. I thank you again for your input on the matter, Rose, as it's given me some perspective on the matter. Given as the group for our Baltimore game isn't as diablerie happy, I doubt it should be as much of an issue with them, as with other venues.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1353-riche","name":"RichE","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T23:41:56-08:00","id":344436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=344037#post344037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably also if they did it by changing the nature of their soul, for example with the help of a sorcerer or mage.</div> </div> </div> </div> Do vampires still have souls that can be manipulated? I remember it as being ambiguous before. Maybe someone can write a blog about it when Mage 2.0 comes out. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T00:20:12-08:00","id":344460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=344436#post344436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do vampires still have souls that can be manipulated? I remember it as being ambiguous before. Maybe someone can write a blog about it when Mage 2.0 comes out. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if they still have souls that can be diablerized... ;p I think the only splat where we truly have to worry about the ambiguity of a soul is Changeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1353-riche","name":"RichE","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T00:32:03-08:00","id":344461,"title":"","content":"All depends on the setting. My old &quot;version&quot; of it was that the reason no one could manipulate a vampires soul in the traditional manner was that theirs was their blood, imbued with life, power and twisted echoes of their original one. Even had an NPC in one game who experimented with it, though he failed horribly and just managed to create a sort of blood creature that hunted kindred.<br /> If that works, go with it, if that doesn't &quot;fit&quot; for you say they have a normal one. As for the 2nd ed canon... not sure what it is, Rose or one of the more well-read members on this board might?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T07:11:33-08:00","id":344678,"title":"","content":"This is a question directed at Rose, mainly: <br /> <br /> how valid is an interpretation of Vampire: the Requiem in which the protagonists aren't <span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">resurrected - but instead things inhabiting corpses that only think they are the person in question (with the assorted issues of identity and all)? </span></span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T07:28:26-08:00","id":344692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=344678#post344678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a question directed at Rose, mainly:<br /> <br /> how valid is an interpretation of Vampire: the Requiem in which the protagonists aren't <span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">resurrected - but instead things inhabiting corpses that only think they are the person in question (with the assorted issues of identity and all)? </span></span></span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>As valid as any interpretation? I don't think they're in the habit of telling you something is wrong for your game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T07:44:02-08:00","id":344700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=344678#post344678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a question directed at Rose, mainly:<br /> <br /> how valid is an interpretation of Vampire: the Requiem in which the protagonists aren't <span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">resurrected - but instead things inhabiting corpses that only think they are the person in question (with the assorted issues of identity and all)? </span></span></span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I have that as one of the rumors around Clan Gangrel, they are just demons (or Strix) posesing corpses and taking on the personality and memories of the former host. As they advance in Protean the fa\u00e7ade starts to crack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T12:55:04-08:00","id":345055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=344678#post344678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a question directed at Rose, mainly:<br /> <br /> how valid is an interpretation of Vampire: the Requiem in which the protagonists aren't <span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">resurrected - but instead things inhabiting corpses that only think they are the person in question (with the assorted issues of identity and all)? </span></span></span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I love games that ask questions about identity! Got lots of mileage out of that with both <i>Demon</i> games. And that's an interesting way to look at it.<br /> <br /> But by the books, vampires are the same people they were before they died. That makes characters like Bruise Minor easy to identify with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T12:59:35-08:00","id":345057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=344678#post344678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a question directed at Rose, mainly:<br /> <br /> how valid is an interpretation of Vampire: the Requiem in which the protagonists aren't <span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">resurrected - but instead things inhabiting corpses that only think they are the person in question (with the assorted issues of identity and all)? </span></span></span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>you could do that and say that you are playing a Strix that forgot what he is and belives he is a vampire","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T06:36:10-08:00","id":345726,"title":"","content":"So, in my little group, we had been saying that called shots to the head and various things like exceptional successes with longsword attacks and whathaveyou bypass the &quot;lethal damage does bashing&quot; rule and just does lethal. However, last night I happened upon the rules for damage again, and didn't see anything like this.<br /> <br /> Do Vampires truly only take bashing from lethal sources except for specific exceptions (kindred dueling 3 and protean claws) or are there rules for general exceptions that I'm missing? Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T10:00:42-08:00","id":345824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=345726#post345726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, in my little group, we had been saying that called shots to the head and various things like exceptional successes with longsword attacks and whathaveyou bypass the &quot;lethal damage does bashing&quot; rule and just does lethal. However, last night I happened upon the rules for damage again, and didn't see anything like this.<br /> <br /> Do Vampires truly only take bashing from lethal sources except for specific exceptions (kindred dueling 3 and protean claws) or are there rules for general exceptions that I'm missing? Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires only take bashing damage from mundane sources that usually deal lethal damage, like guns or knives. The exception is massive trauma, like getting hit by a truck.<br /> <br /> I've never tried dealing lethal damage on exceptional successes, and that would shift around the balance of combat beyond what we playtested. When the new edition was in development, I considered having certain called shots be exceptions to damage downgrading, but it seemed too fiddly to make the default. I also didn't want to make called shots seem mandatory.<br /> <br /> That said, sometimes I consider head wounds and such massive trauma. If a vampire gets a sword through an eye or something and they're not using Resilience, it'd feel off to me for it not to be lethal. But that's something I do pretty occasionally and depends heavily on the narrative part of combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T20:04:00-08:00","id":346364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TittoPaolo210</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=342404#post342404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Theban Sorcery requires you to have a minimum humanity because it works with your rational human mind, the part of you that dreams, that makes plan, that cares and, most of all, has the power to believe (whereas the beast cares only about safety and blood), the farther away you get from that enlightened state of mind the harder it is for the power of your beliefs to call that higher power that gives you miracles and that pure state of mind of true belief is also something you can't steal with diablerie.</div> </div> </div> </div> Here is My problem. Theban has ritual that lets you kill someone and raise them as a zombie for info.Literally Necromancy. How does that fit Vampiric blood magick that has ties to the man?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T02:16:30-08:00","id":346544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=346364#post346364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Here is My problem. Theban has ritual that lets you kill someone and raise them as a zombie for info.Literally Necromancy. How does that fit Vampiric blood magick that has ties to the man?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because Theban Sorcery imitates human thaumaturgy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","name":"Audrey St. John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T05:48:40-08:00","id":346591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=345824#post345824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, sometimes I consider head wounds and such massive trauma. If a vampire gets a sword through an eye or something and they're not using Resilience, it'd feel off to me for it not to be lethal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you consider a heart shot (not a stake, just like bullets or blades or whatever else that hit dead-on) to be appropriate for that, considering the metaphysical importance of the organ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T05:15:52-08:00","id":347330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=345824#post345824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That said, sometimes I consider head wounds and such massive trauma. If a vampire gets a sword through an eye or something and they're not using Resilience, it'd feel off to me for it not to be lethal. But that's something I do pretty occasionally and depends heavily on the narrative part of combat.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Not really. Even humans can survive having their eyes gouged out, they're not a vital organ, after all. Besides, vampires don't bleed out unless they want to bleed out. Now if the blade kept going through and out the other side, that's different, since it might slice through the brain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T10:26:38-08:00","id":347518,"title":"","content":"Personally I houserule any damage to the brain and heart as lethal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T11:24:38-08:00","id":347537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=346364#post346364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Here is My problem. Theban has ritual that lets you kill someone and raise them as a zombie for info.Literally Necromancy. How does that fit Vampiric blood magick that has ties to the man?</div> </div> </div> </div>Theban Sorcery walks a very precarious thematic tightrope. It draws upon dreams, enlightenment, human will, and the purity of a higher belief. These are things we generally consider safer, more amenable, things that better the world.<br /> <br /> Put them in the hands of an unliving monster and see what you get. Sometimes, when the Man wrests control from the Beast and wields the occult power of the blood for its own purer purposes, the result sparks hope. Sometimes, you have merely traded the danger of a wild animal for that of a cold judge. The Man, too, can dream awful things to force the blood to conjure.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T13:14:07-08:00","id":347638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=347330#post347330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Not really. Even humans can survive having their eyes gouged out, they're not a vital organ, after all. Besides, vampires don't bleed out unless they want to bleed out. Now if the blade kept going through and out the other side, that's different, since it might slice through the brain.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's what I meant. In the actual game, the weapon went through the character's eye and out the back of his skull.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T15:54:21-08:00","id":347798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=345824#post345824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vampires only take bashing damage from mundane sources that usually deal lethal damage, like guns or knives. The exception is massive trauma, like getting hit by a truck.<br /> <br /> I've never tried dealing lethal damage on exceptional successes, and that would shift around the balance of combat beyond what we playtested. When the new edition was in development, I considered having certain called shots be exceptions to damage downgrading, but it seemed too fiddly to make the default. I also didn't want to make called shots seem mandatory.<br /> <br /> That said, sometimes I consider head wounds and such massive trauma. If a vampire gets a sword through an eye or something and they're not using Resilience, it'd feel off to me for it not to be lethal. But that's something I do pretty occasionally and depends heavily on the narrative part of combat.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks for the response! That seems like a fantastic way to handle things. As a follow-up question, does the damage type magic/supernatural attacks get downgraded to bashing depending on the power? I notice that abilities in Second Edition specifically say when they cause lethal to even Kindred (Protean and such), so didn't know if all powers should be treated that way across gamelines or not. Or is it a case-by-case, ST-judgement sort of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T16:32:47-08:00","id":347839,"title":"","content":"Question: If one were to adapt the Adoption Rules from Strange Dead Love to B7S would adoption or leaving a lineage cost a WP dot or point?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-27T18:04:18-08:00","id":352138,"title":"","content":"Would vampires be able to temporarily see the Shadow/Spirit Realm by drinking werewolf blood? What other werewolf abilities could be assimilated? Do you have to drink a lot of their blood? Or would that require some sort of ritual?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-27-2014, 09:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-27T18:53:05-08:00","id":352192,"title":"","content":"By RAW in 2e, we have no mention of special effects from any kind of blood. If you think it'd be interesting as an effect in your game, by all means, feel free to give them some kind of Twilight Sight for Spirits or something.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't have drinking Werewolf blood give werewolf abilities or anything like that, though. No blood gives you any abilities on its own. If you're Diablerizing someone, it's not the blood, it's their soul. You can only Diablerize vampires, so it's not very applicable.<br /> <br /> If you want suggestions for cool effects, I'd either do twilight vision or make them suffer a penalty to frenzy for the rest of the scene. Werewolf blood carries some of that <i>kuruth </i>in it or whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-27T18:57:30-08:00","id":352195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=352192#post352192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By RAW in 2e, we have no mention of special effects from any kind of blood. If you think it'd be interesting as an effect in your game, by all means, feel free to give them some kind of Twilight Sight for Spirits or something.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't have drinking Werewolf blood give werewolf abilities or anything like that, though. No blood gives you any abilities on its own. If you're Diablerizing someone, it's not the blood, it's their soul. You can only Diablerize vampires, so it's not very applicable.<br /> <br /> If you want suggestions for cool effects, I'd either do twilight vision or make them suffer a penalty to frenzy for the rest of the scene. Werewolf blood carries some of that <i>kuruth </i>in it or whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for answering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-28T09:50:26-08:00","id":352779,"title":"","content":"In regards to the environmental tilts Extreme Cold (0/32 degrees) and Extreme heat (40/104 degrees), the tilts cause Supernaturals to heal at half their normal rate, and get penalties for every hour they're affected, and eventually damage.<br /> <br /> Do vampires ignore this? I could see them not feeling as uncomfortable, but a vampire seems like it would be affected in some way standing in freezing temperatures for hours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-28-2014, 12:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-28T10:19:45-08:00","id":352824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=352779#post352779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do vampires ignore this? I could see them not feeling as uncomfortable, but a vampire seems like it would be affected in some way standing in freezing temperatures for hours.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I wouldn't take it past Bashing damage, at most, as frostbite causes cellular rather than grossly anatomic damage. Even soft tissue damage caused by a vampire trying to move with frozen veins and muscles wouldn't be the kind of load-bearing damage that Lethal requires, IMO. I'd imagine that using Blush of Life would cut down on those two consequences even further.<br /> <br /> If you wanted to get really cruel, it might cut into your Vitae by destroying red blood cells. Considering how blood volume and vitae quantity are no longer related, though, as long as you've got a few unfrozen ounces left <i>somewhere </i>you could probably get by without concern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1289,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","user":"Hastur00","date":". 12-28-2014, 01:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T00:56:02-08:00","id":359986,"title":"","content":"I have a question, if I may:<br /> <br /> Both my ST and I like the Danse Macabre Masquerade/Dirge merits, but we're at a loss on how to translate the cost reduction properties on these merits. Any advice on how to proceed? 2e. costs for disciplines and merits look a bit hard to lower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Historian ~ <b><a href=\"http://www.nwodbrasil.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.cronistasdastrevasbr.com</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>I currently ST a... </b>MtAW 2e campaign called &quot;Axis Mundi - Si Vis Pacem&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/250-yuukale","name":"Yuukale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T01:38:00-08:00","id":360015,"title":"","content":"Instead of reducing the cost, give out one beat whenever the condition is met. (that is, when they buy whatever would have reduced the cost)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T09:20:17-08:00","id":362533,"title":"","content":"I hope that I am not Hijacking this thread by asking another not so frequently asked question( or two ).<br /> I have been told in other posts or questions that the &quot;flavor text&quot; is not just flavor it is how things are suppose to work. (specifically when I asked about the text in the seductive beast )<br /> <br /> 1: I completely understand that people interpret things differently and I have a tenancy to interpret things literally, which i have done for Professional Training. All the flavor text, even the title of the merit and the title of the dots, Imply that you have been trained by someone else. The very definition of Continuing Education is schooling/ workshops. within my group(s) We have come to a disagreement on what this means. Can you be self taught? could you have gone to the library and read up on things or even just practice? Ultimately can you justify taking this Merit if you have received no professional training, no schooling, no mentoring?<br /> <br /> <br /> 2: Bows are a whole other thing too. Archery is a sport, athletics cover sports. If athletics is thrown weapons, firearms states it's guns and weaponry states it's melee only. Where do you put a bow. In old stuff, it falls under firearms or athletics. But Do you feel that pulling a trigger on a gun, would make you good shooting a bow? Also if you were good with Archery as an athletic sport, would it fall under the same skill as Katniss fighting for her life with the bow? <br /> <br /> 3: How do you feel about stacking specialties? Encouraged? Forbidden? Specific example: Brawl: Fist and Martial arts fighting style. So pretty much whenever she is fighting, two more dice because that would be her chosen method of fighting. Granted their would be situations where fists possibly might not be used or where the merit would not be included in the attack, but more often than not both would apply. I am sure there are other examples to this as well. (long distance shots and rifle ? )<br /> <br /> 4: Faces in the crowd: Title and specifically in the description it states when you are in a crowd. I Have read over the thread where individuals have discussed where and when it can be used. Like a military base when people are milling about. getting through security at check points ect. My question is. what if there is no crowd? No one to blend in with. Sure you are in a public park where people are allowed to be, but you and Joe Human are the ONLY ones there. Are you still unnoticed? That defeats the entire description of the ability. Or say If you hold someone's hand does the person know who they are with, but everyone ignore it?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T10:38:08-08:00","id":362638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=362533#post362533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope that I am not Hijacking this thread by asking another not so frequently asked question( or two ).<br /> I have been told in other posts or questions that the &quot;flavor text&quot; is not just flavor it is how things are suppose to work. (specifically when I asked about the text in the seductive beast )<br /> <br /> 1: I completely understand that people interpret things differently and I have a tenancy to interpret things literally, which i have done for Professional Training. All the flavor text, even the title of the merit and the title of the dots, Imply that you have been trained by someone else. The very definition of Continuing Education is schooling/ workshops. within my group(s) We have come to a disagreement on what this means. Can you be self taught? could you have gone to the library and read up on things or even just practice? Ultimately can you justify taking this Merit if you have received no professional training, no schooling, no mentoring?</div> </div> </div> </div>Flavor text and rules are not an absolute separation. That said, it's important to recognize that Merits are also an abstraction and that there's some room for interpretation on how one acquires particular Merits. Notably, Professional Training has stuff like &quot;Thug&quot; and &quot;Vagrant&quot; and I doubt you'll necessarily be receiving your training from the Department of Thuggery &amp; Vagrancy at the University of Hard Knocks.<br /> <br /> My suggestion for characters that might not be getting formally trained any longer is that they still in same way engage with their profession or people related to it, regardless of circumstances. That's how they keep those skills so sharp. The Contacts are one of the little ways you can facilitate that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=362533#post362533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2: Bows are a whole other thing too. Archery is a sport, athletics cover sports. If athletics is thrown weapons, firearms states it's guns and weaponry states it's melee only. Where do you put a bow. In old stuff, it falls under firearms or athletics. But Do you feel that pulling a trigger on a gun, would make you good shooting a bow? Also if you were good with Archery as an athletic sport, would it fall under the same skill as Katniss fighting for her life with the bow?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fencing and many other things may also be considered a sport, don't let that be the sole determinant of which skill you'd use with Archery. Personally, I'd use Firearms, but it's up to your group whether they'd do that or not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=362533#post362533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3: How do you feel about stacking specialties? Encouraged? Forbidden? Specific example: Brawl: Fist and Martial arts fighting style. So pretty much whenever she is fighting, two more dice because that would be her chosen method of fighting. Granted their would be situations where fists possibly might not be used or where the merit would not be included in the attack, but more often than not both would apply. I am sure there are other examples to this as well. (long distance shots and rifle ? )</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be more creative than that. Punching is fine because you won't get it during Grappling and situations where you'd narrate it as kicking, or when your Arms get wracked. I'd apply Martial Arts when doing something that involves one of the Maneuvers, like making a Called Shot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=362533#post362533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4: Faces in the crowd: Title and specifically in the description it states when you are in a crowd. I Have read over the thread where individuals have discussed where and when it can be used. Like a military base when people are milling about. getting through security at check points ect. My question is. what if there is no crowd? No one to blend in with. Sure you are in a public park where people are allowed to be, but you and Joe Human are the ONLY ones there. Are you still unnoticed? That defeats the entire description of the ability. Or say If you hold someone's hand does the person know who they are with, but everyone ignore it?</div> </div> </div> </div>It works automatically if there's a crowd or if people aren't scrutinizing you. I think this is also the official word on it, but what I've made it mechanically is that when you use it it's generally more difficult for people to notice you. So they suffer your Obfuscate dots as a penalty to Perception checks to notice you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 01-07-2015, 01:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T10:49:58-08:00","id":362686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=362533#post362533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope that I am not Hijacking this thread by asking another not so frequently asked question( or two ).</div> </div> </div> </div>Impossible! This thread cannot be hijacked. Our defenses are impregnable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=362533#post362533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have been told in other posts or questions that the &quot;flavor text&quot; is not just flavor it is how things are suppose to work. (specifically when I asked about the text in the seductive beast )</div> </div> </div> </div>The most important thing to remember is just to apply common sense. That cuts both ways. It means that if a power that says that it seduces a character succeeds, that character ought to act seduced, but it also means that an interpretation that your group agrees is properly in the spirit of a power ought to be acceptable even if a strict reading of the power doesn't cover it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=362533#post362533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1: I completely understand that people interpret things differently and I have a tenancy to interpret things literally, which i have done for Professional Training. All the flavor text, even the title of the merit and the title of the dots, Imply that you have been trained by someone else. The very definition of Continuing Education is schooling/ workshops. within my group(s) We have come to a disagreement on what this means. Can you be self taught? could you have gone to the library and read up on things or even just practice? Ultimately can you justify taking this Merit if you have received no professional training, no schooling, no mentoring?</div> </div> </div> </div>Professional Training exists to incentivize fleshing out your character and providing plot hooks to hang on. Your professional connections are one of those hooks: you're hooked into your profession and benefit from the aid and advice of your fellows, but that means that something interesting happening to one of your contacts is a tool in your ST's toolbox. Rule it as such. For example, a self-taught musician who doesn't join jam sessions or perform gigs, but merely practices a lot in seclusion, might be a virtuoso with a high Expression rating, but he's unlikely to have access to the networking and mentorship that Professional Training provides. Conversely, a lot of computer hackers are going to have learned by doing rather than having attended any special classes or received formal training, but they're going to have learned in part by communicating with other hackers and learning from what's gone before them, so such a hacker is likely fit to benefit from Professional Training.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=362533#post362533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2: Bows are a whole other thing too. Archery is a sport, athletics cover sports. If athletics is thrown weapons, firearms states it's guns and weaponry states it's melee only. Where do you put a bow. In old stuff, it falls under firearms or athletics. But Do you feel that pulling a trigger on a gun, would make you good shooting a bow? Also if you were good with Archery as an athletic sport, would it fall under the same skill as Katniss fighting for her life with the bow?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a situational call and depends on how often you expect the use of bows to show up in your game. Archery involves a lot of compensation and strength that doesn't translate over to the use of firearms, but having Firearms as a separate skill to its own also relates to the World of Darkness's general positioning in the modern genre. If people aren't drawing guns a lot then a single Projectiles skill covering both guns and bows seems fit enough. If there's a lot of gunplay involved, but one character has arisen from the past, trained before the widespread use of firearms, then they might use the Athletics skill instead to distinguish them further. If you're playing a historical game set during the fall of the Camarilla, you might just wholly convert the Firearms skill into an Archery skill. None of these decisions particularly break the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=362533#post362533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3: How do you feel about stacking specialties? Encouraged? Forbidden? Specific example: Brawl: Fist and Martial arts fighting style. So pretty much whenever she is fighting, two more dice because that would be her chosen method of fighting. Granted their would be situations where fists possibly might not be used or where the merit would not be included in the attack, but more often than not both would apply. I am sure there are other examples to this as well. (long distance shots and rifle ? )</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I'd be fine with stacking so long as the specialties are interesting in their own right. &quot;Good at using my fists&quot; is not a very interesting specialization and situations that would rule it out are relatively far between. If you had, say, specialties in &quot;agile fighting&quot; and &quot;aikido,&quot; then sure, great, when you're defending yourself with throws and flips and you have a lot of space to move around in, go nuts. As a general rule, you want Venn diagrams that can have significant overlap but aren't just one big circle with a little outline on the edges.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=362533#post362533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4: Faces in the crowd: Title and specifically in the description it states when you are in a crowd. I Have read over the thread where individuals have discussed where and when it can be used. Like a military base when people are milling about. getting through security at check points ect. My question is. what if there is no crowd? No one to blend in with. Sure you are in a public park where people are allowed to be, but you and Joe Human are the ONLY ones there. Are you still unnoticed? That defeats the entire description of the ability. Or say If you hold someone's hand does the person know who they are with, but everyone ignore it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, it's situational. The power works by blending you into the back of memory as not worth noticing or remembering. If you're just passing Joe Human in the park not doing anything, I'd allow it; even without a herd to blend into, that's a situation where it's not uncommon for Joe Human to walk past somebody without noticing anything about them. Separate observers make separate checks to notice the vampire when she interacts with something in a way that might draw attention, so you can be noticed by one person and not by others, though if the one person then points you out I'd say that'd probably break your cover.<br /> <br /> I haven't read the thread in question so interpretations there may vary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T07:13:00-08:00","id":363467,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=362638#post362638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Notably, Professional Training has stuff like &quot;Thug&quot; and &quot;Vagrant&quot; and I doubt you'll necessarily be receiving your training from the Department of Thuggery &amp; Vagrancy at the University of Hard Knocks.<br /> <br /> My suggestion for characters that might not be getting formally trained any longer is that they still in same way engage with their profession or people related to it, regardless of circumstances. That's how they keep those skills so sharp. The Contacts are one of the little ways you can facilitate that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand that there are no schools for thugs and Vagrants, but think of gangs and mob hierarchy, a lot of them have mentors or people to work with to show them the ropes. Could I just read a book on how a gang is suppose to work then say that I am a professional gang member? That was my point. Can I be completely self taught and take this? How would I get contacts if I just ran to the library or watched how to videos? Think of it this way. if I wanted to be a professionally trained engineer and I learned on my own. What are my chances of getting a real job as an engineer without the schooling to reflect that? Or even a Gang thug, I cant just walk up to them and expect to be part of their world. Even if you were a professionally trained con artist, I still see having the need to have a mentor or some sort of Other person teaching you.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=362686#post362686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Conversely, a lot of computer hackers are going to have learned by doing rather than having attended any special classes or received formal training, but they're going to have learned in part by communicating with other hackers and learning from what's gone before them, so such a hacker is likely fit to benefit from Professional Training.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not saying All, but I am saying A good deal of hackers went to school or in high school took classes for computer programs. Also, I would think that actively communicating with other hackers, asking advice how to ect is getting some sort of mentorship and not going at it alone. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=362638#post362638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It works automatically if there's a crowd or if people aren't scrutinizing you. I think this is also the official word on it, but what I've made it mechanically is that when you use it it's generally more difficult for people to notice you. So they suffer your Obfuscate dots as a penalty to Perception checks to notice you.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you were walking alone down a street and someone else was walking alone down the other side, wouldnt you watch them, look at them and wonder why they are there alone? Even more so what if they had a bazooka? How can you be just another face in the crowd if there isnt a crowd? I would think that being on a deserted street, in a park or building calls attention in and of itself. Or perhaps that is my human curiosity wanting to know why the heck the other person is there all alone late at night. wondering if they are wondering the same thing about me?!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=362686#post362686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I'd be fine with stacking so long as the specialties are interesting in their own right. &quot;Good at using my fists&quot; is not a very interesting specialization and situations that would rule it out are relatively far between. If you had, say, specialties in &quot;agile fighting&quot; and &quot;aikido,&quot; then sure, great, when you're defending yourself with throws and flips and you have a lot of space to move around in, go nuts. As a general rule, you want Venn diagrams that can have significant overlap but aren't just one big circle with a little outline on the edges.</div> </div> </div> </div>(Specific example to follow and should the other read this, my apologies. I am just trying to better my understanding of how things work ) My character's background was that he was a professional boxer for a few years and simply enjoyed fighting for the sake of fighting. ( Hense, specialty when using his fists, I think I worded it on the sheet as Boxing? I dont recall now. ) then I took the merit Martial Arts fighting style for the extra fun things to do while swinging his fists, there comes the specialty in that. Then I think I took my third specialty in... Called shots? Or.. Um All out attack or something? Eeep! I dont remember. Anyway I was told to change one of the Fist or Martial arts because they would always stack. So I did, because one shouldnt argue with the ST ^.^, but it just got me wondering if it was an acceptable thing to do, if it fits the character concept.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=362686#post362686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't read the thread in question so interpretations there may vary.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thread just talked about public places where people should be. I didnt add there, because this is a separate scenario where no one is around except 1 observer and 1 vampire with obfuscate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T10:39:45-08:00","id":363672,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=363467#post363467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand that there are no schools for thugs and Vagrants, but think of gangs and mob hierarchy, a lot of them have mentors or people to work with to show them the ropes. Could I just read a book on how a gang is suppose to work then say that I am a professional gang member? That was my point. Can I be completely self taught and take this? How would I get contacts if I just ran to the library or watched how to videos? Think of it this way. if I wanted to be a professionally trained engineer and I learned on my own. What are my chances of getting a real job as an engineer without the schooling to reflect that? Or even a Gang thug, I cant just walk up to them and expect to be part of their world. Even if you were a professionally trained con artist, I still see having the need to have a mentor or some sort of Other person teaching you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, hopefully people's explanations for having Professional Training is a bit more involved than just reading a book anyway. We can't give you guidelines for every situation, but I think a good general rule is that a Profession has to be or have been a big, significant part of your life to translate to having those merit dots. My character with Professional Training (Thug) has been loyal to the crew for a long time. My character with Professional Training (Lawyer) went to Law School and worked at a firm for years. That sort of thing. If you're taking Professional Training for something, it, in my opinion, should be embedded into your background solidly, because it means you're a professional in that arena. Spending many years on the streets as a homeless individual, just scraping by with occasional help from your fellows might entitle one to Professional Training (Vagrant) for instance, which isn't as formal. There's just room for that sort of interpretation.<br /> <br /> Just, y'know, again, whatever it is, it should be something that a character has spent a lot of time with. You don't get Professional Training (Lawyer) from being a hobbyist that watches <i>Law &amp; Order</i>. You get it from a not insignificant amount of time with hands on experience.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=363467#post363467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not saying All, but I am saying A good deal of hackers went to school or in high school took classes for computer programs. Also, I would think that actively communicating with other hackers, asking advice how to ect is getting some sort of mentorship and not going at it alone.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you guys are agreeing here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=363467#post363467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you were walking alone down a street and someone else was walking alone down the other side, wouldnt you watch them, look at them and wonder why they are there alone? Even more so what if they had a bazooka? How can you be just another face in the crowd if there isnt a crowd? I would think that being on a deserted street, in a park or building calls attention in and of itself. Or perhaps that is my human curiosity wanting to know why the heck the other person is there all alone late at night. wondering if they are wondering the same thing about me?!</div> </div> </div> </div>That'd be why I wouldn't make it automatically succeed, I'd require that Perception check, penalized by their Obfuscate dots. If you fail the check, you just don't really notice the person. If you do, you notice them fully, with the range of possible action that might entail. It's a supernatural power, so the notion that it might supernaturally affect your natural instinct to intensely scrutinize the only other person walking down the street doesn't seem too far out of the question, with absolute invisibility within two dots reach.<br /> <br /> This way, Obfuscate 1's utility isn't solely limited to being in a crowd, while it's simultaneously not the perfect stealth offered by Obfuscate 3. It serves a different purpose. If you're using Obfuscate 3 you can just walk into the house. Obfuscate 1 would then make it easier to sneak in, but still require that sneaking.<br /> <br /> Let me stress also that <b><i>*this is a House Rule*</i></b> and is a comfortable one for my table. What works for yours may not be the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T11:35:44-08:00","id":363714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=363672#post363672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That'd be why I wouldn't make it automatically succeed, I'd require that Perception check, penalized by their Obfuscate dots. If you fail the check, you just don't really notice the person. If you do, you notice them fully, with the range of possible action that might entail. It's a supernatural power, so the notion that it might supernaturally affect your natural instinct to intensely scrutinize the only other person walking down the street doesn't seem too far out of the question, with absolute invisibility within two dots reach.<br /> <br /> This way, Obfuscate 1's utility isn't solely limited to being in a crowd, while it's simultaneously not the perfect stealth offered by Obfuscate 3. It serves a different purpose. If you're using Obfuscate 3 you can just walk into the house. Obfuscate 1 would then make it easier to sneak in, but still require that sneaking.<br /> <br /> Let me stress also that <b><i>*this is a House Rule*</i></b> and is a comfortable one for my table. What works for yours may not be the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tossed that Idea at a couple of our group members and we like that house rule too. ^.^<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T13:38:08-08:00","id":364741,"title":"","content":"Time for another crazy question! Or not so crazy, really. But anyhoo, it says in the rules for the Vinculum that once someone hits the 3rd stage, all stages from other blood bonds disappear. Does this mean they are immune to getting 1st or 2nd stage bonds from other vamps in future? Or can they still have lower level bonds even after they have been fully bonded to their regnant?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1353-riche","name":"RichE","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T13:55:31-08:00","id":364753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichE</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=364741#post364741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Time for another crazy question! Or not so crazy, really. But anyhoo, it says in the rules for the Vinculum that once someone hits the 3rd stage, all stages from other blood bonds disappear. Does this mean they are immune to getting 1st or 2nd stage bonds from other vamps in future? Or can they still have lower level bonds even after they have been fully bonded to their regnant?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No further bonds can be formed until the third stage bond dissolves. No first, second, or third.<br /> <br /> 'Once the bond reaches the third stage, it shatters all other existing bonds, and prevents further bonds from forming.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T20:59:10-08:00","id":366005,"title":"","content":"So, let's say that a member of the Malleus Maleficarum member becomes Embraced. He would then lose access to Benedictions, wouldn't he (though he'd get the merit points back)? I assume adding the Vampire template axes the Hunter template, and thus removes anything the Hunter had that required being a Hunter, but I'm having some trouble finding the lines in any book pointing to Templates and how you would lose a minor Template upon gaining a major one, etc. Anyone know where that stuff is at?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T21:12:36-08:00","id":366010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=366005#post366005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, let's say that a member of the Malleus Maleficarum member becomes Embraced. He would then lose access to Benedictions, wouldn't he (though he'd get the merit points back)? I assume adding the Vampire template axes the Hunter template, and thus removes anything the Hunter had that required being a Hunter, but I'm having some trouble finding the lines in any book pointing to Templates and how you would lose a minor Template upon gaining a major one, etc. Anyone know where that stuff is at?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's way back in Second Sight. Hopefully the new 2e core rules will have an updated sidebox or something for it.<br /> <br /> 'When a character transitions from one of this book\u2019s lesser templates to a full template, he loses the supernatural abilities he gained from the lesser template. This is a rule of the game, however, not a rule of the supernatural cosmos of the World of Darkness.'<br /> <br /> It goes on to suggest that this might explain having a strange out-of-clan discipline upon Embrace. And it has a loose guideline for what would later become Sanctity of Merits, suggesting they get full or half-experience points refunded for things they didn't use to 'buy in' to specialize their supernatural template. The specific example given has a woman who turns into a Mekhet, and gains some ranks of Dominate due to her using her psychic powers to do similar things pre-Embrace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-11-2015, 12:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T21:48:34-08:00","id":366042,"title":"","content":"Ahhhh, Second Sight. Was looking through GMC, the Corebook, Vampire, and a few Hunter books. There we go.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":274,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","user":"Enokh","date":". 01-11-2015, 01:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T19:15:08-08:00","id":369296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=366010#post366010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It's way back in Second Sight. Hopefully the new 2e core rules will have an updated sidebox or something for it.<br /> <br /> 'When a character transitions from one of this book\u2019s lesser templates to a full template, he loses the supernatural abilities he gained from the lesser template. This is a rule of the game, however, not a rule of the supernatural cosmos of the World of Darkness.'<br /> <br /> It goes on to suggest that this might explain having a strange out-of-clan discipline upon Embrace. And it has a loose guideline for what would later become Sanctity of Merits, suggesting they get full or half-experience points refunded for things they didn't use to 'buy in' to specialize their supernatural template. The specific example given has a woman who turns into a Mekhet, and gains some ranks of Dominate due to her using her psychic powers to do similar things pre-Embrace.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> There is one exception but is within the same line. Ghouls when embraced get to keep their disciplines.<br /> Though They probably loose the new Blood and Smoke ghoul merits.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T13:11:21-08:00","id":370054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=366005#post366005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, let's say that a member of the Malleus Maleficarum member becomes Embraced. He would then lose access to Benedictions, wouldn't he (though he'd get the merit points back)? I assume adding the Vampire template axes the Hunter template, and thus removes anything the Hunter had that required being a Hunter, but I'm having some trouble finding the lines in any book pointing to Templates and how you would lose a minor Template upon gaining a major one, etc. Anyone know where that stuff is at?</div> </div> </div> </div>One little point, though. <i><b>Hunters are not Templates</b></i>...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T15:39:19-08:00","id":370220,"title":"","content":"I'd let a vampire keep Benedictions. Probably Castigation, too, since we referred to that one as &quot;in the blood.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T13:12:37-08:00","id":371385,"title":"","content":"So what you mean to tell us is... according to the lore of the Lucifuge the way they tell it and the Testament Of Longinus, the Dark Prophet was the same as them. He was a Lucifuge, before they were known by that name. His dark gifts were not Theban Sorcery. They were Castigations blessed in his destined Damnation with even more terrible power.<br /> <br /> And what Saint Daniel did that day to cloud the sky and rip through the pagan armies wasn't just Theban Sorcery. It was Theban Sorcery tempered in the blood of the Adversary. Explaining why no one has been able to replicate its sheer glory since. For the line of the Monachus carried the blood of Longinus, who carried the blood of Christ in death and the Adversary in life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T13:33:29-08:00","id":371403,"title":"","content":"Hunter Endowments likely respond very differently to supernatural changes. Advanced Armory, for example, is just gear that requires a chip. If the transformation into a supernatural leaves said chip intact than the character could probably still use whatever gear he possesses... unless the chip checks for life signs then there might be a problem.<br /> <br /> About half of the hunting groups have physical stuff: gear, potions, relics, special blood, etc. The rest are more ambiously empowered.<br /> <br /> Spinning off of the Castigation idea, that's not a bad concept for a Hunter antagonist group. A rough cell of the Lucifuge have realized that one of their number being Embraced counts as them being dead for total Lucifuge allowed at any one time, allowing more members to awaken to their power at any one time and have dedicated themselves to Embracing their own kind in an attempt to swell their numbers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/785-full-time-gm","name":"Full Time GM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar785_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T14:26:32-08:00","id":371455,"title":"","content":"From a game standpoint, it works best to just say nothing transfers, from there Storytellers know they can bend the rules where they want. Otherwise you could say your vampire was a member of the Aegis Kai Doru and so he has artifacts, or she was a member of the Ascending Ones, so she can make ointments or whatever, which a Storyteller wasn't ready for and now has to tell the player no, and the player can point at the rules and say there's no rule against it.<br /> <br /> But from a story standpoint, when you're running the game and feel fine with it or playing the game if you know your ST, and hopefully they're open minded, and your characters are growing (or being killed as they get Embraced) it's not unreasonable to let them keep their abilities or pick relevant other abilities. I don't particularly like the transferring of telepathy to Auspex myself, and would probably just let them keep their telepathy, especially considering how cool the idea of psychic vampires is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T16:58:19-08:00","id":371554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=370220#post370220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd let a vampire keep Benedictions. Probably Castigation, too, since we referred to that one as &quot;in the blood.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's a very interesting take! I agree with nofather, as well, in that there's certainly a difference between a character creating a Vampire and trying to get away with having Hunter powers than there is someone actively playing a Hunter that got Embraced. There's also the angle of &quot;World of Darkness is full of weird shit hiding in the corners of everywhere, why not with Vampires and such?&quot;. All exciting responses.<br /> <br /> Also, as always, I'm gonna go fanboy-out in the corner over having Rose respond to something I posted. This place is the best.<br /> <br /> (I just finished reading The Strix Chronicle Anthology you lot are the best ever)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T17:52:48-08:00","id":371614,"title":"","content":"Joshua Alan Deutsh, writer of Lullay and Strangeness in the Proportion, knocked Neil Gaiman off his post for my favorite author with the former work.<br /> <br /> <i>Neil Freaking Gaiman</i>, folks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T19:50:27-08:00","id":371726,"title":"","content":"I loved Lullay, I guess Strangeness is next on the list, then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T20:05:00-08:00","id":371734,"title":"","content":"Heh. Ascending Ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T21:05:46-08:00","id":371774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=371614#post371614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Joshua Alan Deutsh, writer of Lullay and Strangeness in the Proportion, knocked Neil Gaiman off his post for my favorite author with the former work.<br /> <br /> <i>Neil Freaking Gaiman</i>, folks.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I don't know whether to be highly honored as a writer...or violently offended as a Gaiman fan.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#990000\">Joshua Alan Doetsch</span></b><br /> <b>Freelance Writer<br /> <a href=\"http://joshuadoetsch.com/\" target=\"_blank\">joshuadoetsch.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1054-scrivnomancer","name":"scrivnomancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1054_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T08:20:24-08:00","id":372559,"title":"","content":"Why not both?<br /> <br /> EDIT: I might encourage the violence because I've been misspelling your last name for ages though. I don't know where that u comes from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T08:21:02-08:00","id":372560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=371554#post371554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's a very interesting take! I agree with nofather, as well, in that there's certainly a difference between a character creating a Vampire and trying to get away with having Hunter powers than there is someone actively playing a Hunter that got Embraced. There's also the angle of &quot;World of Darkness is full of weird shit hiding in the corners of everywhere, why not with Vampires and such?&quot;. All exciting responses.<br /> <br /> Also, as always, I'm gonna go fanboy-out in the corner over having Rose respond to something I posted. This place is the best.<br /> <br /> (I just finished reading The Strix Chronicle Anthology you lot are the best ever)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah. And Cancer cells are a thing, after all. Makes one wonder if Belial's Brood aren't a bunch of Les Infants Diabolique or whatever that ended up getting embraced. Though Castigations is less demonic powers, and more rites created by the Lucifuge to Hunt demons, so maybe not quite the same...<br /> <br /> I found Rose's thoughts on the matter a bit iffy at first, as it sounds like mixing stuff in a way which could rapidly become quite OP (Vampires slinging fireballs at each other, anyone?), but, as I said before, Cancer Cells are a thing. Guess it all depends on how the fluff of it is treated in a game where such a thing is implemented, so that it creates for interesting story, as opposed to just Vamps with laser beams and BEES! For reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1353-riche","name":"RichE","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T14:16:32-08:00","id":372870,"title":"","content":"Can I hijack this to ask two questions? I do t wanna waste space on the forum. Or more like, two explainations?<br /> <br /> 1) what's the deal with the ventrue curse? They're just more likely to loose their touchstone?<br /> <br /> 2) I don't understand level 5 majesty at all. I thought I did but the last paragraph makes it sound like it's talking about two vampires. At least to be it does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T14:39:36-08:00","id":372898,"title":"","content":"1) there's numerous threads asking this question. You can find at least a couple of discussions if you google it using this site as a site to look in.<br /> 2) Supercharged Awe. Anyone affected by Awe get's affected by Majesty 5 and has problems doing anything bad to the vampire, as the description says.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T17:53:10-08:00","id":373132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichE</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=372560#post372560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...as opposed to just Vamps with laser beams and BEES! For reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires already <i>get </i>bees.<br /> <br /> ...<i>uhhuhhuhgh</i>. *shudder*<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T18:27:59-08:00","id":373179,"title":"","content":"Bees. My god.<br /> <br /> I suppose vampires would make for a good cause for Amazonian myth.<br /> <br /> Anyways, fingerprints. I've heard people say vampires don't leave them because being dead, no oils from their finger pads. So Blush of Life would cause you to leave fingerprints where you touched?<br /> <br /> One of the characters in my last game was a thief and I'm surprised I haven't heard tales of other vampire non-homicidal criminals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T19:14:31-08:00","id":373220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=373179#post373179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bees. My god.<br /> <br /> I suppose vampires would make for a good cause for Amazonian myth.<br /> <br /> Anyways, fingerprints. I've heard people say vampires don't leave them because being dead, no oils from their finger pads. So Blush of Life would cause you to leave fingerprints where you touched?<br /> <br /> One of the characters in my last game was a thief and I'm surprised I haven't heard tales of other vampire non-homicidal criminals.</div> </div> </div> </div>In <i>New Wave Requiem </i>it briefly discusses Vampires and forensic evidence in the 1st edition. Back then it was that it was much harder to get fingerprints, since the only way you could get them would be from things besides natural oils leaving them behind. I think it was either a -3 or -5 to rolls to try to collect fingerprints left by a vampire, with an Obfuscate Devotion that made it harder/impossible.<br /> <br /> I think you could choose on an individual basis, but I'd likely rule that Blush of Life would cause you to leave fingerprints. It'd be more interesting that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T22:41:22-08:00","id":373328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hastur00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=373132#post373132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vampires already <i>get </i>bees.<br /> <br /> ...<i>uhhuhhuhgh</i>. *shudder*</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> lol, I was trying to quickly come up with a piece of Thaumatech that Vamps don't already have access to through disciplines, but I guess I was going more for comedy with that particular choice. xD Maybe some of the more obscure ones from Hunter supplements, if we're looking at weird stuff Vamps can't do. Even then, probably still a short list. The stuff that counters magic seems about the only truly out there thing, I suppose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1353-riche","name":"RichE","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T14:10:16-08:00","id":373759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichE</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=373328#post373328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but I guess I was going more for comedy with that particular choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Comedy achieved <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-18T09:12:07-08:00","id":374291,"title":"","content":"If vampires' skin were completely dry without the Blush of Life, it'd make them feel awfully weird to the touch. Not very good for makeout feeding....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-18T15:52:28-08:00","id":374523,"title":"","content":"Well, without blush of life they are cold so... still not very good for makeout feeding?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-19T02:44:29-08:00","id":375061,"title":"","content":"Question regarding the Strix: When a strix's living host takes enough damage to kill them, they switch to the &quot;possess corpse&quot; rules. What happens to the health track? Because when they possess a corpse directly they presumably start with a clean one despite the corpse having been in a similar state when it, y'know, died.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-19T03:12:40-08:00","id":375092,"title":"","content":"I'd say it gets a new clean Health track. Terrifing, isn't it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-19T03:18:56-08:00","id":375095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=374291#post374291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If vampires' skin were completely dry without the Blush of Life, it'd make them feel awfully weird to the touch. Not very good for makeout feeding....</div> </div> </div> </div>Imagine how the &quot;dry eyes&quot; from Req 1.0 fiction would feel. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-19T05:18:49-08:00","id":375167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=375061#post375061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question regarding the Strix: When a strix's living host takes enough damage to kill them, they switch to the &amp;quot;possess corpse&amp;quot; rules. What happens to the health track? Because when they possess a corpse directly they presumably start with a clean one despite the corpse having been in a similar state when it, y'know, died.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say it depends on whether or not the Health track is filled with Aggravated damage or Lethal. That would be why dismemberment, disintegration, or immolation of a Strix's host are effective tactics straight out of the gate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","name":"Audrey St. John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-19T06:15:32-08:00","id":375206,"title":"","content":"If the host is killed it had to be filled with Aggravated Damage or else is not killed at all. You die when the last Health Box is marked with Aggravated and not before that. Of course if the body was beheaded that would count as dead even if the Health track was not full, but then a Strix cannot posess a beheaded corpse, or can they?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-19T06:24:35-08:00","id":375214,"title":"","content":"The book says that the host is killed at all lethal and <i>destroyed</i> at all aggravated, but like you said that's not how it works for a non-possessed human. <br /> <br /> I think the issue is that a full track of aggravated in a mortal usually means &quot;irreparable organ failure&quot; rather than &quot;actually smashed to bits&quot;. We're trying to model two different things with the same trait.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-19T09:06:17-08:00","id":375297,"title":"","content":"I see... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> ...still prefer the shock of having an antagonist again at full capacity after the coterie thought it was all over, so if it ever happens in my chronicles (my New Orleans one ended last Saturday <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />) I probably rule clean Health track.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-19T09:41:36-08:00","id":375320,"title":"","content":"Oh, yeah, I agree with that bit completely. It's just a question of <i>when.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-19T18:41:30-08:00","id":375752,"title":"","content":"During our vampire game I spent some time pondering certain dominate commands and I was curious about what the rulings would be for these issued in a fight.<br /> 'You beat me.' - Do you think, providing the fight wasn't to the death, this would end it?<br /> 'I beat you.' - Same question.<br /> 'I ran away.' or 'I went that way.' - Would they chase after 'you' or would they shrug as if you had gotten away, ignoring you momentarily?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-19-2015, 10:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-20T05:40:22-08:00","id":376088,"title":"","content":"Don't see why this wouldn't work. If you can make people believe you were never there (as per the book) you can certainly make them believe you were there but are now running off in a certain direction. At which point they would either go after &quot;you&quot; or wander off, their fight concluded. I don't see a problem with the other two uses either. I'd much rather have a Ventrue getting out of a fight in a clever way like that then try some awkward victim-hurts-himself schemes or whatever. It takes two turns to pull off (1 instant to establish, 1 instant to give command) so it's not very useful if there's more than one opponent anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-20T06:45:13-08:00","id":376155,"title":"","content":"I would think inflicting the mesmerized condition would end the fight. Those statements would provide a good explanation for why the fight ended so the victim wouldn't be suspicious as to their fuzzy recollection of the fight. I think 'I went that way' would then require the vampire to get out of sight to be effective. It could wait until the vampire was done mind melting. I don't think dominate can manage 'you can't see me.' <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-20T08:12:30-08:00","id":376261,"title":"","content":"Inflicting the mesmerized condition does absolutely nothing to your behavior. The subsequent command changes the behavior <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> As for &quot;i'm running off&quot; i'd say that fails too. you can give orders, you can manipulated his memories (I ran away, is good, tho).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-20T21:34:24-08:00","id":376904,"title":"","content":"Well, it does <i>something</i> to a person's behavior. They stop what they might have been doing to await a command. Otherwise a person would just look away and break contact. That is just common sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T02:20:46-08:00","id":377064,"title":"","content":"Iron Edict does that. Mesmerize does not, that's one of its primary weaknesses. That said once Mesmerized you don't need to look into the eyes to give orders, just speak (that's why an Exceptional Success is such a big deal).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T04:54:32-08:00","id":377121,"title":"","content":"Nothing about the Mesmerized condition says you need to maintain eye contact. Else it would have &quot;Resolution: The Vampire looks away.&quot; You only need eye contact to inflict Mesmerized, after that you're free to turn your back on the guy you Mesmerized (though until you give a command he's in full control, if feeling a bit muted) and just speak your commands loud enough that they can still hear. Do some somersaults while you're at it, Mesmerized don't care, Mesmerized don't give a shit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T06:04:13-08:00","id":377135,"title":"","content":"So the box under Dominate that says:<br /> Eye Contact<br /> Dominate requires a vampire make eye contact<br /> with her victims in order to issue commands.<br /> <br /> Doesn't apply to mesmerize? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The condition also has:<br /> You\u2019re not obviously hypnotized \u2014 you\u2019re a bit quiet and reserved<br /> compared to normal, but nothing out of the ordinary.<br /> <br /> If normal is punching the vampire in the face, reserved would have to be <i>not</i> punching the vampire in the face. If the person is shooting at the vampire and gets mesmerized then they should stop shooting, but they would continue to have the gun pointed at the vampire. In combat people tend to get tunnel vision and it would be difficult to argue that most people under most circumstances would actually be looking anywhere near an opponent's eyes so actually getting mesmerize to work while fighting is a problem. If it does work then I really don't see how a mesmerized person can continue fighting in a quiet and reserved manner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":". 01-21-2015, 09:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T06:22:05-08:00","id":377141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=377135#post377135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the box under Dominate that says:<br /> Eye Contact<br /> Dominate requires a vampire make eye contact<br /> with her victims in order to issue commands.<br /> <br /> Doesn't apply to mesmerize? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>No, what Unahim said was, you only need the eye contact to inflict Mesmerized. <b>Once the target is mesmerized</b> you do not need to continue maintaining eye contact.<br /> <br /> The <i>Eye Contact</i> side bar and the description of the <i>Mesmerized </i>condition seem to disagree, though. The side bar says you need to maintain eye contact when you issue the commands, while the Mesmerized condition says nothing of the sort.<br /> <br /> Going by classical vampire fiction, though, eye contact is necessary for issuing commands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T06:31:45-08:00","id":377163,"title":"","content":"It says they need to <i>make</i> eye contact, not <i>maintain </i>it. My impression was that one brief glance was enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T15:22:21-08:00","id":377561,"title":"","content":"While I think it's good to do whatever works best for your game, when I've seen Dominate-like mesmerism in fiction/vampire films, they tend to maintain eye contact when issuing the command, and that strikes me as dramatically appropriate. I'd advise people to go that route with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T19:16:37-08:00","id":378604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=377135#post377135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the box under Dominate that says:<br /> Eye Contact<br /> Dominate requires a vampire make eye contact<br /> with her victims in order to issue commands.<br /> <br /> Doesn't apply to mesmerize? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The condition also has:<br /> You\u2019re not obviously hypnotized \u2014 you\u2019re a bit quiet and reserved<br /> compared to normal, but nothing out of the ordinary.<br /> <br /> If normal is punching the vampire in the face, reserved would have to be <i>not</i> punching the vampire in the face. If the person is shooting at the vampire and gets mesmerized then they should stop shooting, but they would continue to have the gun pointed at the vampire. In combat people tend to get tunnel vision and it would be difficult to argue that most people under most circumstances would actually be looking anywhere near an opponent's eyes so actually getting mesmerize to work while fighting is a problem. If it does work then I really don't see how a mesmerized person can continue fighting in a quiet and reserved manner.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;...but nothing out of the ordinary&quot; for you means stopping in the middle of a fight? Sure, alright <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Your &quot;what is and isn't reserved&quot; line is pure fiction. Maybe reserved means I'm punching you in the face without yelling about how you enjoy putting phalluses in your mouth. Making a dodgy argument at best here.<br /> <br /> I do agree about the tunnel vision part, though. At our table dominate generally just does not function once the gloves have come off.<br /> <br /> Others have posted valid points concerning the rest of what you have posted, so I'll refrain from just repeating things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=377561#post377561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I think it's good to do whatever works best for your game, when I've seen Dominate-like mesmerism in fiction/vampire films, they tend to maintain eye contact when issuing the command, and that strikes me as dramatically appropriate. I'd advise people to go that route with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whether you need to maintain eye contact or not doesn't change whether or not the victim is forced not to act right away, of course. I'd say that if you go down that route just disallowing the use in active combat situations is probably a good idea. When things aren't tense it makes sense for them to keep looking into your eyes, but if they're all movement, fists and feet then I have trouble imagining you standing there putting your attention (instant action, after all) into looking at the other guy's eyes in the vague hope he'll reciprocate and then catching him in whatever split-second that he does it in, then stopping him cold that way. Strikes me as more dramatically appropriate when the guy relying on Dominate for everything loses control of the situation if he carelessly blows it up, anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":1292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","user":"Unahim","date":". 01-22-2015, 10:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-23T04:49:28-08:00","id":378893,"title":"","content":"I think once initiative is rolled you'd need to get the guy in a grapple or something and <i>force</i> him to look at you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-23T05:18:59-08:00","id":378918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=378604#post378604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;...but nothing out of the ordinary&quot; for you means stopping in the middle of a fight? Sure, alright <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Your &quot;what is and isn't reserved&quot; line is pure fiction. Maybe reserved means I'm punching you in the face without yelling about how you enjoy putting phalluses in your mouth. Making a dodgy argument at best here.</div> </div> </div> </div>It means other observers don't consider your withdrawn behavior due to being Mesmerized for the rest of the scene to be out of the ordinary.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/reserved\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/reserved</a><br /> <br /> Mesmerized Condition.<br /> <br /> Your character\u2019s will is subordinate to that of a vampire. You\u2019re not obviously hypnotized \u2014 you\u2019re a bit quiet and reserved compared to normal, but nothing out of the ordinary. (Blood and Smoke p. 305)<br /> <br /> <br /> Saying being afflicted with the Mesmerized Condition allows you to continue assaulting the person who mesmerized you while screaming about sucking dicks in direct contradiction of the definition of the word reserved because others don't consider your behavior out of the ordinary is beyond dodgy, it's utter horseshit. Just like claiming its impossible to establish eye contact in a fight is garbage. Because unless you're blind, you're watching your opponent in a fight and all a Dominate user requires is one second of eye contact to Mesmerize someone.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":190,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","user":"Audrey St. John","date":". 01-23-2015, 08:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","name":"Audrey St. John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-23T06:34:27-08:00","id":378968,"title":"","content":"Which is why you always fight a Ventrue with help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-23T06:45:49-08:00","id":378976,"title":"","content":"I say that if a victim is aware that they're fighting a vampire, like some of the hunters my players have been fighting, then the vampire has to grapple and force eye contact to initialize Mesmerize, but ignorant victims don't think to look away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-23T07:19:26-08:00","id":379008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Audrey St. John</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=378918#post378918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Saying being afflicted with the Mesmerized Condition allows you to continue assaulting the person who mesmerized you while screaming about sucking dicks in direct contradiction of the definition of the word reserved because others don't consider your behavior out of the ordinary is beyond dodgy, it's utter horseshit.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is utter horseshit is your ability to read, maybe you shouldn't throw words like that around until you can at least understand what is being said. I said Mesmerise would certainly prevent you from doing that. I guess the word &quot;without&quot; is the one you have trouble understanding. Since you're &quot;charming&quot; enough to provide dictionary links (douchebag tactic #1), let me reciprocate:<br /> <a href=\"http://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/without\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/without</a><br /> <br /> As you said, others don't consider your withdrawn behaviour out of the ordinary. Since stopping in the middle of a fight certainly would be out of the ordinary, you obviously do not do that. Unless you claim that Dominating someone changes the perception of all the non-dominated people, which I find laughable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just like claiming its impossible to establish eye contact in a fight is garbage. Because unless you're blind, you're watching your opponent in a fight and all a Dominate user requires is one second of eye contact to Mesmerize someone. </div> </div> </div>You don't tend to watch the eyes, that's not what telegraphs the opponent's moves most. Maybe you only need one second of eye contact, but there's also reaction time to consider, unless the person is just &quot;beaming&quot; Dominate non-stop or something. I've been in enough fights (competitive and otherwise) and you certainly wouldn't be dominating me during a &quot;turn&quot; most of the time. You might get lucky at a slip up one turn out of five, but anyway. Supposedly you're dodging my blows, too. That one second I look is likely to be that one second you're really going to get your face caved in if you don't cover it right now.<br /> <br /> Now, if you can't keep inflammatory language out of your next post, please do me a favour and don't bother. You're just pissing me off that way (if you can't tell) rather than inviting proper discussion. Wish I could just stay cool about it, but there's way too many people who think it's ok to run off their mouth at people who don't agree with them over here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":1292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","user":"Unahim","date":". 01-23-2015, 10:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-23T13:08:39-08:00","id":379437,"title":"","content":"When deciding if you can continue punching someone who Mesmerized you unless they order you otherwise, it's not the &quot;reserved&quot; line you should be looking at. It's the fact that the condition is called Mesmerized, the first line saying &quot;Your character\u2019s will is subordinate to that of a vampire.&quot; and the part about &quot;not obviously hypnotized&quot; which implies that you ARE hypnotized. You are mesmerized and hypnotized, which means you wait for orders. You will is subordinated, which means you don't make your own decisions. Ergo, if we assume you can use Dominate in a fight, inflicting the Mesmerized Condition ends that fight.<br /> <br /> The &quot;you\u2019re a bit quiet and reserved compared to normal, but nothing out of the ordinary&quot; part isn't there to explain what you do in the short lapse of time between getting Mesmerized and getting orders. It's there to say that <i>while following orders</i>, you don't look like a zombie, staring slack-jawed ahead and obviously under someone's control. You appear relatively normal, just quiet. Of course, if someone saw you getting hypnotized, they're going to think your actions are out of the ordinary no matter how you act.<br /> <br /> Or at least, that's my interpretation.<br /> <br /> As for the eye contact thing, the way I see it is that while breaking eye contact doesn't break Mesmerized, you need to establish it to inflict the Condition, and you need to hold it to give orders. In between those, you can do whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-23T14:05:49-08:00","id":379501,"title":"","content":"And we interpret it differently. You get mesmerized, your will is subordinate, but until the order is given it is not shifted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-23T14:43:10-08:00","id":379525,"title":"","content":"To join in the dictionary trend, to mesmerize means to capture someone's attention completely. It certainly makes sense to me that you'd stop whatever you were doing.<br /> <br /> But ah, well, not a big deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-23T19:24:57-08:00","id":379758,"title":"","content":"No need for anyone to get pissy. I agree with Kazorh when it comes to interpretations. I can accept that I was unclear on a few points. I thought it was a given that once mesmerized a person's will is no longer their own. The condition doesn't indicate what the requirements are to issue commands so there is no conflict with the side bar. According to the side bar, you need eye contact to issue commands to a mesmerized person. A person would remain mesmerized without eye contact but would not accept commands without it. This is a fairly trivial matter.<br /> <br /> The issue with splitting hairs between a subordinate will and a shifted will, if you accept there is a difference, is apparent when you consider the consequences. If a person is antagonistic to the vampire then they would close their eyes and cover their ears to avoid hearing any commands once mesmerized <i>if</i> they are able. If the person is allowed to continue to act on their own until given an order then they are able to avoid commands. Mesmerize becomes meaningless in many situations. I don't believe this would demonstrate a subordinate will.<br /> <br /> In this niche case of dominate during combat, if you want to get technical and say a person would not stop in mid punch after being mesmerized then that is fair. If you say that a person will continue to attack (as an action on a turn) until told specifically to stop then you force the above situation where mesmerize is useless. It is unlikely the vampire would want to be attacked. Unless ordered to do so then why would a mesmerized person with a will subordinate to the vampire continue to attack the vampire? Mesmerized does not mean lose all mental faculties (as in &quot;derp, me dumb&quot;). A mesmerized person should move out of the way of an attack unless ordered not to. A mesmerized person should not attack people that are not enemies without an order. Once mesmerized the vampire is no longer an enemy (suborned will).<br /> <br /> I think mesmerize should be difficult, not impossible, during combat. It takes some time (turn) so unless a vampire is giving up defending to mesmerize they should get penalties or go to special effort as BigDamHero suggested. This is something that should be handled depending on the exact situation rather than some blanket rule, IMO. I might say &quot;try it, but you only get a chance die.&quot; I wouldn't say it just won't work. If the need to cripple mesmerize to prevent killing a story by its use during combat, there are better means of prevention.<br /> <br /> I guess I shouldn't have tried brevity before. *sigh* Everyone is free to do as they please and accept the problems that might result. There is no utility in allowing a mesmerized person to act differently than a hypnotized person. I don't mean deep hypnosis, but the state inflicted by mentalists that leaves people fully hypnotized and susceptible to suggestion, but still able to react to stimuli normally. I say that is what the mesmerized condition is. If you could hypnotize someone as they were attacking you then they would cease their attacks without needing to be told. The person would act to defend themselves then according to what they believe their controller wants then do nothing until given instructions, unless acting on given instructions.<br /> <br /> The key factor with mesmerize is the interaction between the vampire and the victim. Other people's perceptions are a distant concern. If the mesmerized will continue an action or initiate new actions, which includes taking an attack action, then serious consideration should be given to how this affects the vampire/victim interaction. Is the mesmerized really acting as if their will is the same as the vampire's, as best as they know it? That is the question that needs to be answered. A mesmerized person could continue to act if the answer to the question is yes. They would not act against the vampire's interest on their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-24T02:35:22-08:00","id":379922,"title":"","content":"Well, you'd need to use celerity to actually <i>interrupt</i> a punch. So as far as doing without that goes I could see an argument about the mesmerising being slipped in during a lull in the motion or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-24T10:06:14-08:00","id":380255,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'd say it's a Manipulation + Subterfuge or Brawl roll, tops. Chances are you could do it by just saying &quot;my character stops, straightens up out of their fighting stance, crosses their arms, and smiles slyly&quot;. Unless their opponent is <i>really</i> focused on wafflestomping them into the ground, or the combat is clearly life-or-death, they'll probably pause that critical moment out of confusion and/or suspicion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T08:14:39-08:00","id":381987,"title":"","content":"Ok, so does Meditation work as written in the core book, under the GMC rules update?<br /> <br /> Does it apply to Humanity under Requiem 2nd Edition rules?<br /> <br /> And if you're a mortal with the second level of the Meditative Mind merit, when you roll an Integrity check does the +3 bonus to Resolve + Composure checks supersede the basic +1 bonus when rolling a degeneration check?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4837-imajica1863","name":"imajica1863","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T09:43:42-08:00","id":382107,"title":"","content":"Yes.<br /> <br /> ST's fiat. I'd allow it myself since mechanically the specific mechanic you are referring to is about coming to terms with what you are but the Humanity isn't Integrity mantra is just as valid as an excuse to disallow it. There are also other benefits to being able to immediately enter a meditative trance which is why I would permit it.<br /> <br /> I stack them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","name":"Audrey St. John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T13:38:56-08:00","id":382244,"title":"","content":"Guys, can a discipline's passive power fulfill prerequisites for merits? Say, resilience providing extra stamina and allowing the vampire to buy merits for which he wouldn't be able without having resilience?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Historian ~ <b><a href=\"http://www.nwodbrasil.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.cronistasdastrevasbr.com</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>I currently ST a... </b>MtAW 2e campaign called &quot;Axis Mundi - Si Vis Pacem&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/250-yuukale","name":"Yuukale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T15:16:03-08:00","id":382355,"title":"","content":"It didn't in first edition but now it's permanently on I don't know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T20:14:51-08:00","id":382655,"title":"","content":"Very simple, very stupid question:<br /> Does the Nosferatu's clan bane (Lonely Curse) which makes all presence and manipulation failures turn into dramatic failures also applies to Intimidate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3873-hirogawa","name":"hirogawa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T03:14:59-08:00","id":382844,"title":"","content":"I would say no. The curse makes them scary as hell, that's why they tend to be avoided or rejected.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T03:43:14-08:00","id":382866,"title":"","content":"As Written - Applies to Intimidate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T04:00:06-08:00","id":382899,"title":"","content":"True, if you diregard all the paragraph preceding that: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vampire: the Requiem 2nd ed. P.103</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nosferatu embody fear, disgust, and all manner of uncomfortable feelings. Some are inhumanly ugly. Some have a gaze that makes a person feel violated.</div> </div> </div> </div> Remember that that's also part of the rules. You really think such a monster would usually fumble intimidation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T04:14:10-08:00","id":382911,"title":"","content":"The whole premise of Promethean is they're so uncomfortable and disgusting that humans can take up arms to destroy it. <br /> So fumbling intimidation might just as well happen to nosferatu. <br /> <br /> And obviously, of course, such a monster would NOT usually fumble intimidation. And this monster will usually pack an Intimidation score which will make it a rarity. And if his monstrous ugly face helps, then most likely some Striking Looks for Inimidation as well making the chance for this failure quite miniscule...<br /> If you build your character in another direction, and you ignore Initmidation skill then why not? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T05:20:19-08:00","id":382967,"title":"","content":"The old bane explicitly didn't apply to intimidation, so it feels weird that this one is more ambiguous about it. <br /> <br /> Of course, a dramatic failure could be interpreted as them reacting in a way the vamp didn't intend. Maybe you try to intimidate someone to do something and they just run off screaming instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T05:22:54-08:00","id":382969,"title":"","content":"Or perhaps they are more open to what a Nosferatu is and how they are strange this time around? Does every Nosferatu need to be scary? Well, Nightmare and Vigor probably suggest yes... but what about those creepy voyeurs who stalk you, are creepy, but are not scary?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T07:18:38-08:00","id":383069,"title":"","content":"Well... that makes absolutely no sense... I mean, the whole concept of the Nosferatu are about being scary as hell, even their unique Discipline focuses on that. That penalty applying to Intimidation breaks the whole concept and outright makes them very shitty at the only social thing they should care about, or even be good at. Nightmare 1 let's them apply their Nightmare score to mundane Intimidation rolls, what's the point of that if you're passive to fumbling those rolls?<br /> Makes no sense, man..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3873-hirogawa","name":"hirogawa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T07:45:54-08:00","id":383099,"title":"","content":"Allow me to assist with this. If you turn to page 106 of Blood and Smoke, you see the Humanity rules. If you go down a bit, you will see the following text; &quot;These modifiers apply to rolls relating to humans. Manipulating humans for food with Subterfuge or frightening them with Intimidation are not affected; but trying to understand a human's emotional cues with the Empathy skill would be affected.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now, if you turn to page 103 for the Lonely Curse; &quot;When dealing with humans, treat the Nosferatu's Humanity as two dots lower for the purpose of Social penalties.&quot;<br /> <br /> So, as written, the Nosferatu curse follows the exact same rules as Humanity, just treated as being 2 dots lower when &quot;relating to humans&quot;, and it's not so simple as just &quot;social penalties&quot;. Thus Intimidation is exempt from the drawbacks, as is Subterfuge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1353-riche","name":"RichE","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T08:04:37-08:00","id":383117,"title":"","content":"That makes sense and it might have been RAI.<br /> <br /> What hirogawa is saying however... is every Daeva by default a socially good character? No. Is every Nosferatu a scary one? Once again it's a no. <br /> &quot;outright makes them very shitty at the only social thing they should care about&quot; is complete exaggeration. if you're such a scary mofo, then you won't be failing those rolls in any frequence. Add in the Nightmare (if you raised it) and you're likely to be rolling huge dice pools.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T08:08:08-08:00","id":383120,"title":"","content":"I'm mostly referring to the later part of the Lonely Curse which states: treat any Presence and Manipulation failures as dramatic failures.<br /> This basically says that even with Nightmare boosting your dice pools every Intimidation test you roll with Presence and Manipulation has a strong chance of going terribly awry. Basically your only social skill, the only one you SHOULD EXCEL AT, is a russian roulette.<br /> This does not apply to Kindred or Touchstones, but even so, most your interactions should be with regular humans. I'm just picturing a guy trying to feed of a young girl, popping out of the shadows with his creppy face, summoning some crazy and scary illusions, only to have a dramatic fail on the dice and having the young girl laugh her ass off while she walks away from the creepy guy.<br /> Makes. No. Sense.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3873-hirogawa","name":"hirogawa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T08:12:02-08:00","id":383121,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I agree with that, completely. And I think that's the RAI. <br /> <br /> But a strict reading of the RAW applies the penalty <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T12:50:11-08:00","id":383462,"title":"","content":"&quot;if you're such a scary mofo, then you won't be failing those rolls in any frequence. Add in the Nightmare (if you raised it) and you're likely to be rolling huge dice pools. &quot;<br /> Dude... I've seen a player roll 20 die before he got 1 success (he didn't roll all those dices in the same test, he added up all the dices until he got a success but still). I would be way more cool with that if I had any reason to trust in the dice averages. But I don't, so yeah...<br /> That's still freaking nuts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3873-hirogawa","name":"hirogawa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T13:09:27-08:00","id":383482,"title":"","content":"It's called a <i>dramatic </i>failure. Trying to scare someone and having them laugh at you isn't dramatic. Trying to scare someone and having them flip out and try to attack you is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T09:05:21-08:00","id":404524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yuukale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=382244#post382244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guys, can a discipline's passive power fulfill prerequisites for merits? Say, resilience providing extra stamina and allowing the vampire to buy merits for which he wouldn't be able without having resilience?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I kind of want to bump this question by Yuukale because it has me kinda curious myself. On the one hand, I don't see why not? I mean, the passive effects are pretty much always on, and nothing short of discipline nulling powers (there must be some out there, by now) would stop the Vampire from benefiting from those stat increases. But on the other, hmmmm... well, suppose it depends entirely on whether a stat increased by a power counts for the purposes of merit prerequisites, regardless of whether it's a stat increase (as opposed to modifier), or not. Hopefully Rose or David will weigh in on this one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1353-riche","name":"RichE","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T13:12:44-08:00","id":404991,"title":"","content":"*in my best Rose's voice* Not by default, but it doesn't break things to allow this.<br /> <br /> You wouldn't find many people willing to allow blood buffing to count towards a prerequisite, or equipment bonuses, etc. However, the physical disciplines were written to encourage vampire players to buy discipline dots instead of attribute dots on the average so it wouldn't make much sense to try to swing things back in favor of buying attributes. It seems a pretty straightforward situation. If the power is nullified then the merit can't be used until the power is back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T07:08:00-08:00","id":410055,"title":"","content":"What's the deal with ghouls and resilience? <br /> They can spend vitae to gain armor but the wound still actually happens, even though they receive no damage. They are still mortal so a hole through the chest is still pretty bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2572-hugsworth","name":"Hugsworth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T07:21:03-08:00","id":410069,"title":"","content":"Yeah, they got the hole, but it doesn't negatively impact their survival or actions. Yes, the ghoul has a hole. Yes, it's probably looking pretty bad. Yes, it's gonna heal up after he get's a good night's sleep.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T10:18:08-08:00","id":425383,"title":"","content":"Can you cause a blood bond by injecting your Vitae into someone, like dosing their heroin or something? In the specific case I'm asking about it was put in a syringe with a bunch of tranquilizers to try and incapacitate a werewolf. I know supernaturals can resist it and I think 'dosing' with Vitae was more common in Vampire the Masquerade but I'm not sure if Vampire the Requiem allows for that or if you need the Vitae to be from the source.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T10:43:54-08:00","id":425418,"title":"","content":"Supernaturals don't explicitly get a resist check anymore and if spitting in someone's eye is enough to establish a vinculum, I imagine lacing someone's drugs can count also. But there's nothing specific about how long the vitae retains its potency outside the vampire's body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","name":"Audrey St. John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T11:13:26-08:00","id":425435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Audrey St. John</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=425418#post425418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Supernaturals don't explicitly get a resist check anymore and if spitting in someone's eye is enough to establish a vinculum, I imagine lacing someone's drugs can count also. But there's nothing specific about how long the vitae retains its potency outside the vampire's body.</div> </div> </div> </div>In which instance are you referring to with someone having established a Vinculum by spitting vitae in someone's eye?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1353-riche","name":"RichE","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T11:33:17-08:00","id":425450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=425383#post425383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you cause a blood bond by injecting your Vitae into someone, like dosing their heroin or something? In the specific case I'm asking about it was put in a syringe with a bunch of tranquilizers to try and incapacitate a werewolf. I know supernaturals can resist it and I think 'dosing' with Vitae was more common in Vampire the Masquerade but I'm not sure if Vampire the Requiem allows for that or if you need the Vitae to be from the source.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If you can ghoul these ways, I would say you can form the blood bond as that happens when you ghoul. I have allowed for spiking shots with vitae, i don't see why you can't spike a needle.<br /> <br /> (Edit) Found the reference pg 59:<br /> <br /> A vampire need not press the prospective ghoul\u2019s lips to his wrist. There are so many other ways to skin that cat.<br /> The Serpent bites his lip, and you barely notice the copper in the kiss.<br /> The Haunt spits bloody phlegm in your eye, inexplicably, as you pass on the midnight road. Now you sit in your apartment feeling more afraid than you think you ought to, wondering if you should go get tested for some disease.<br /> You reach for your expensive coffee, but it tastes weird. A Shadow smiles in front of your face, but you cannot see her.<br /> You drank from a chalice when a Lord commanded you to. And now you...no...you don\u2019t quite remember what happened.<br /> The Savage cuts you and then herself, pressing the open wounds together. Something wild surges between.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":".  added the reference quote and.... I fail at spelling 03-02-2015, 03:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T12:11:10-08:00","id":425528,"title":"","content":"I think lacing drugs should be effective. Vitae usually retains its potency until the end of a scene, but if you need it to work longer for plot purposes, then one hour per dot of Blood Potency would work.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh, and you could modify that with sorcery or Merits, if it needs to be a character schtick rather than a one-off event.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 03-02-2015, 03:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T12:14:24-08:00","id":425531,"title":"","content":"I had no problem with it working for the story but I was wondering about the rules after that. In the blood bond section it seems to talk exclusively about drinking, but page 59 seems to make it clear that's not the only way. My ST will chortle in amusement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T14:01:04-08:00","id":425649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/317776-not-so-frequently-asked-questions?p=425450#post425450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If you can ghoul these ways, I would say you can form the blood bond as that happens when you ghoul. I have allowed for spiking shots with vitae, i don't see why you can't spike a needle.<br /> <br /> (Edit) Found the reference pg 59:<br /> <br /> A vampire need not press the prospective ghoul\u2019s lips to his wrist. There are so many other ways to skin that cat.<br /> The Serpent bites his lip, and you barely notice the copper in the kiss.<br /> The Haunt spits bloody phlegm in your eye, inexplicably, as you pass on the midnight road. Now you sit in your apartment feeling more afraid than you think you ought to, wondering if you should go get tested for some disease.<br /> You reach for your expensive coffee, but it tastes weird. A Shadow smiles in front of your face, but you cannot see her.<br /> You drank from a chalice when a Lord commanded you to. And now you...no...you don\u2019t quite remember what happened.<br /> The Savage cuts you and then herself, pressing the open wounds together. Something wild surges between.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Fluffy. Thanks for that!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1353-riche","name":"RichE","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}